{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c75b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":520,"recorded_at":1780531400001035,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9a5-f59b-7f42-bddc-14e3de3b77d9"},"task_id":"01a0c9a5-f59b-7f42-bddc-14e3de3b77d9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9a5-f59b-7f42-bddc-14e3de3b77d9","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/lifecycle.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"sync\"\n6|\t\"time\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/termbind\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n15|)\n16|\n17|// Lifecycle executes the eight tmux lifecycle operations — create,\n18|// attach, status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n19|// terminate-stale, restore — over the structured commands. Five\n20|// operations (create, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n21|// status) delegate to the landed terminstance engine with the tmux\n22|// backend; attach, terminate-stale, and restore — which the engine\n23|// scope gate refuses — execute here over the same landed gates\n24|// (transition matrix, idempotency shapes, authorization, capability\n25|// conferral, receipt and binding stores) plus the tmux backend.\n26|//\n27|// A Lifecycle is constructed whole: every store and function value is\n28|// required (except Sleep/PollInterval, which default, and\n29|// ServerAdmission, which only attach needs). The Execute entry refuses\n30|// before any work when a dependency is missing.\n31|type Lifecycle struct {\n32|\t// RuntimeDir is the tmux runtime directory (<root>/tmux) the\n33|\t// socket derives from.\n34|\tRuntimeDir string\n35|\t// Root is the Runtime IPC root the socket custody verifies.\n36|\tRoot string\n37|\t// Platform selects the sun_path limit.\n38|\tPlatform scalar.Platform\n39|\t// Runner executes the tmux commands.\n40|\tRunner Runner\n41|\t// Receipts is the durable idempotency receipt table.\n42|\tReceipts *terminstance.ReceiptStore\n43|\t// Bindings is the durable bootstrap binding store.\n44|\tBindings *axpane.Store\n45|\t// Attach is the durable attach-client receipt store.\n46|\tAttach *termbind.AttachStore\n47|\t// States is the durable AX-side state memory.\n48|\tStates *InstanceStates\n49|\t// CurrentLease and CurrentGeneration re-read the winning lease\n50|\t// and the validated binding generation at every check point.\n51|\tCurrentLease      func() terminstance.LeaseView\n52|\tCurrentGeneration func() string\n53|\t// Now is the clock.\n54|\tNow func() time.Time\n55|\t// Sleep waits between close-confirm polls. Nil means time.Sleep.\n56|\tSleep func(time.Duration)\n57|\t// PollInterval separates close-confirm polls. Non-positive means\n58|\t// 50 milliseconds.\n59|\tPollInterval time.Duration\n60|\t// ServerAdmission reports the live server attestation the attach\n61|\t// handler binds to the request generation (the P3-A wiring: a\n62|\t// fresh decoy admission refuses here). Nil refuses attach only.\n63|\t// The context carries the operation deadline and the caller's\n64|\t// cancellation: a cooperative admission returns promptly when\n65|\t// it fires, and the attach entry additionally bounds the wait\n66|\t// itself, so even an adapter that ignores cancellation cannot\n67|\t// hold the request past its deadline or commit late.\n68|\tServerAdmission func(ctx context.Context) (RealmAdmission, error)\n69|\t// LocalHostID is the AX host identity the after-restore\n70|\t// composition compares the winning lease holder against. Empty\n71|\t// cannot prove a local win, so the composition parks or offers\n72|\t// remote attach only, never resumes.\n73|\tLocalHostID string\n74|\t// LeaseRefresh attempts the §4.2 mesh lease refresh\n75|\t// (after-restore step 2) under a timeout context. Nil skips the\n76|\t// attempt; a failed attempt also falls back to local knowledge.\n77|\t// Only a successful refresh verifies: the fallback decides\n78|\t// unverified, so it parks instead of resuming.\n79|\tLeaseRefresh func(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (RefreshWinner, error)\n80|\t// MeshRefreshTimeout bounds one refresh attempt. Non-positive\n81|\t// means DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout. The bound is enforced, not\n82|\t// advisory: the entry returns at the deadline even against an\n83|\t// adapter that ignores cancellation, and a late answer never\n84|\t// verifies.\n85|\tMeshRefreshTimeout time.Duration\n86|\t// Hooks observes receipts and effects. Nil disables observation.\n87|\tHooks *terminstance.EngineHooks\n88|\t// RefreshHooks arms the race boundary of the refresh select.\n89|\t// Nil in production.\n90|\tRefreshHooks *RefreshHooks\n91|\t// barrierMu serializes the input-closure ordering contract: the\n92|\t// quiesce report commit, the boundary report commit, and the\n93|\t// attach writable-receipt commit (barrier recheck, client\n94|\t// receipt, returned vector, advisory memory) are mutually\n95|\t// exclusive, so whichever lands first wins and no writable\n96|\t// receipt commits after a durable closure report. The initial\n97|\t// attach fast-path check and the server admission run outside\n98|\t// the lock (admission may block); only the recheck-to-vector\n99|\t// section holds it. The quiesce engine closure runs inside the\n100|\t// lock (its tmux effects return immediately); the boundary wait\n101|\t// runs outside (it blocks on the wrapper signal) and only its\n102|\t// report commit takes the lock. Non-reentrant: hooks firing\n103|\t// inside a locked section must not call Execute. The contract\n104|\t// is in-process: concurrent ax processes racing attach against\n105|\t// quiesce serialize only through the report files, not through\n106|\t// this mutex (bound B42). The vector handoff the contract\n107|\t// covers ends at vector construction: a caller that execs a\n108|\t// pre-quiescence vector after quiescence commits holds a\n109|\t// pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\n110|\tbarrierMu sync.Mutex\n111|}\n112|\n113|// RefreshHooks arms the race boundary of the mesh lease refresh:\n114|// BeforeSelect runs after the adapter launches and before the entry\n115|// selects over the answer and the deadline. A nil hook is a no-op.\n116|// Tests stall past the bound to force the both-ready race\n117|// deterministically: without the stall the deadline arm always wins\n118|// and the answer-path expiry check never triggers.\n119|type RefreshHooks struct {\n120|\tBeforeSelect func()\n121|}\n122|\n123|// DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout bounds the after-restore mesh lease\n124|// refresh when the Lifecycle leaves it unset: five seconds, after\n125|// which the branch proceeds on local knowledge instead of blocking\n126|// forever.\n127|const DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout = 5 * time.Second\n128|\n129|// RefreshWinner is one mesh lease-refresh answer: the winning lease\n130|// tuple and its holder host.\n131|type RefreshWinner struct {\n132|\tLeaseID      string\n133|\tEpoch        uint64\n134|\tHolderHostID string\n135|}\n136|\n137|// OpRequest is one lifecycle operation request: the operation name,\n138|// its closed body, the presented source state, the admitted\n139|// capabilities, and the fencing material (for terminate-stale only).\n140|type OpRequest struct {\n141|\tOperation            string\n142|\tBody                 []byte\n143|\tSource               string\n144|\tAdmitted             terminalbackend.Admitted\n145|\tPresented            fencing.PresentedToken\n146|\tWinner               sessrepo.LeaseSummary\n147|\tHasWinner            bool\n148|\tForceRecovery        bool\n149|\tDiagnosticsPreserved bool\n150|}\n151|\n152|// AttachOutcome is the attach success payload: the client mirror, the\n153|// host-local descriptor, the authorized input boolean, and the\n154|// evidence. The result input boolean always equals the request and the\n155|// authorization; the landed CheckAttachResult proves it on every call.\n156|type AttachOutcome struct {\n157|\tClientMirrorID  string\n158|\tDescriptor      string\n159|\tInputAuthorized bool\n160|\tEvidenceIDs     []string\n161|}\n162|\n163|// OpOutcome is one executed operation: exactly one of Mutation,\n164|// Status, or Attach is set, plus the per-operation success members.\n165|// Mutation is set on every executed mutating path — success and\n166|// coded failure alike, mirroring the engine — and nil only when the\n167|// request was malformed before any result existed.\n168|type OpOutcome struct {\n169|\tOperation              terminalbackend.Operation\n170|\tMutation               *terminstance.Result\n171|\tStatus                 *terminstance.StatusReport\n172|\tAttach                 *AttachOutcome\n173|\tArgv                   []string\n174|\tBinding                *termbind.Binding\n175|\tDescriptor             *string\n176|\tPriorBindingID         string\n177|\tRestoredParked         bool\n178|\tTargetClosed           bool\n179|\tProcessClosed          bool\n180|\tStoreClosed            bool\n181|\tQuiescenceGeneration   string\n182|\tInputClosedAt          string\n183|\tSafeBoundaryEvidenceID string\n184|\tBoundaryObservedAt     string\n185|}\n186|\n187|// Execute runs one lifecycle operation to its outcome. Refusals\n188|// precede side effects: malformed operations, unknown backends, and\n189|// unsafe sockets refuse before any store or tmux interaction. The\n190|// socket custody (before-connect rejection) and length refusal run on\n191|// every operation, because every operation connects.\n192|func (lc *Lifecycle) Execute(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest) (OpOutcome, error) {\n193|\tempty := OpOutcome{}\n194|\tif lc == nil || lc.Runner == nil || lc.Receipts == nil || lc.Bindings == nil ||\n195|\t\tlc.Attach == nil || lc.States == nil ||\n196|\t\tlc.CurrentLease == nil || lc.CurrentGeneration == nil || lc.Now == nil {\n197|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle dependencies\"}\n198|\t}\n199|\toperation, err := terminalbackend.ParseOperation(req.Operation)\n200|\tif err != nil {\n201|\t\treturn empty, err\n202|\t}\n203|\tif _, err := DirectivesFor(operation); err != nil {\n204|\t\treturn empty, err\n205|\t}\n206|\tsocket := SocketPath(lc.RuntimeDir)\n207|\tif err := CheckSocketLength(socket, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n208|\t\treturn empty, err\n209|\t}\n210|\tif err := CheckSocketCustody(socket, lc.Root, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n211|\t\treturn empty, err\n212|\t}\n213|\tswitch operation {\n214|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationCreate:\n215|\t\treturn lc.executeCreate(ctx, req, socket)\n216|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationAttach:\n217|\t\treturn lc.executeAttach(ctx, req, socket)\n218|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationStatus:\n219|\t\treturn lc.executeStatus(ctx, req, socket)\n220|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\n221|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n222|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n223|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n224|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n225|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n226|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale:\n227|\t\treturn lc.executeTerminate(ctx, req, socket)\n228|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRestore:\n229|\t\treturn lc.executeRestore(ctx, req, socket)\n230|\tdefault:\n231|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle operation\"}\n232|\t}\n233|}\n234|\n235|// engineFor builds the per-call landed engine over a request-scoped\n236|// tmux backend. The engine is a plain struct: constructing one per\n237|// call keeps request identity out of shared state.\n238|func (lc *Lifecycle) engineFor(reqBackend *backend) *terminstance.Engine {\n239|\treturn &terminstance.Engine{\n240|\t\tStore:             lc.Receipts,\n241|\t\tBackend:           reqBackend,\n242|\t\tCurrentLease:      lc.CurrentLease,\n243|\t\tCurrentGeneration: lc.CurrentGeneration,\n244|\t\tNow:               lc.Now,\n245|\t\tHooks:             lc.Hooks,\n246|\t}\n247|}\n248|\n249|// requestBackend builds the request-scoped tmux backend over the\n250|// lifecycle stores and the admitted set.\n251|func (lc *Lifecycle) requestBackend(req OpRequest, socket, session, instance string) *backend {\n252|\tsleep := lc.Sleep\n253|\tif sleep == nil {\n254|\t\tsleep = time.Sleep\n255|\t}\n256|\tpoll := lc.PollInterval\n257|\tif poll <= 0 {\n258|\t\tpoll = 50 * time.Millisecond\n259|\t}\n260|\treturn &backend{\n261|\t\trunner:     lc.Runner,\n262|\t\truntimeDir: lc.RuntimeDir,\n263|\t\tsocket:     socket,\n264|\t\tsessionID:  session,\n265|\t\tinstanceID: instance,\n266|\t\tnow:        lc.Now,\n267|\t\tsleep:      sleep,\n268|\t\tpoll:       poll,\n269|\t\tadmitted:   req.Admitted,\n270|\t\tbindings:   lc.Bindings,\n271|\t\tattach:     lc.Attach,\n272|\t\tstates:     lc.States,\n273|\t\tkillExit:   -1,\n274|\t}\n275|}\n276|\n277|// recordAfter records the adopted after-state in the AX-side memory on\n278|// success paths. The memory is advisory everywhere: status\n279|// reconciles the live probe against it, but attach admission never\n280|// consults it — only the incarnation-scoped closure proof decides\n281|// admission, so a stale or lost memory record can neither reopen a\n282|// closed barrier nor close an open one. On the barrier successes\n283|// (quiesce-input and wait-safe-boundary) the caller still checks the\n284|// returned error and fails closed, keeping the status memory\n285|// faithful to the closure the operation just proved.\n286|func (lc *Lifecycle) recordAfter(instance string, after terminalbackend.InstanceState) error {\n287|\tif lc.States == nil {\n288|\t\treturn nil\n289|\t}\n290|\treturn lc.States.Record(instance, after)\n291|}\n292|\n293|// recordFailure records the after-state of a failed operation. A\n294|// failure with committed effects and an uncertain tail (After\n295|// unavailable) overwrites with the honest unknown: the prior record\n296|// no longer describes the instance. A pure refusal proves nothing —\n297|// its After echoes the caller-carried source — so it installs that\n298|// echo only when the memory holds no record at all (letting the\n299|// uncertain-resume path reconcile a first-operation failure) and\n300|// never overwrites an authoritative record with stale caller state.\n301|// Failure reporting can never reopen a closed barrier: attach\n302|// admission never consults this memory, and a refusal either\n303|// preserves the prior record, installs a first echo, or records the\n304|// non-admitting unknown.\n305|func (lc *Lifecycle) recordFailure(instance string, after terminalbackend.InstanceState) {\n306|\tif lc.States == nil {\n307|\t\treturn\n308|\t}\n309|\tif after == terminalbackend.StateUnavailable {\n310|\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(instance, after)\n311|\t\treturn\n312|\t}\n313|\t_, found, err := lc.States.Lookup(instance)\n314|\tif err != nil || found {\n315|\t\treturn\n316|\t}\n317|\t_ = lc.recordAfter(instance, after)\n318|}\n319|\n320|// mutationResult assembles a lifecycle result with the engine's\n321|// buildResult contract: repeated request identities, before/after\n322|// states, bytewise-sorted effects and evidence, and one disposition.\n323|func mutationResult(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, before, after terminalbackend.InstanceState, effects []terminalbackend.SideEffect, evidence []string, disposition terminstance.RetryDisposition) terminstance.Result {\n324|\treturn terminstance.Result{\n325|\t\tOperationID:           mctx.OperationID,\n326|\t\tSessionID:             mctx.SessionID,\n327|\t\tTerminalInstanceID:    mctx.TerminalInstanceID,\n328|\t\tTerminalBackendID:     mctx.TerminalBackendID,\n329|\t\tImplementationVersion: mctx.ImplementationVersion,\n330|\t\tProtocolVersion:       mctx.ProtocolVersion,\n331|\t\tBackendGeneration:     mctx.BackendGeneration,\n332|\t\tBefore:                before,\n333|\t\tAfter:                 after,\n334|\t\tEffects:               sortedEffects(effects),\n335|\t\tEvidenceIDs:           sortedEvidence(evidence),\n336|\t\tDisposition:           disposition,\n337|\t}\n338|}\n339|\n340|// checkLifecycleBackend admits exactly the tmux backend identity: this\n341|// lifecycle executes for ax.tmux and no other backend. A request\n342|// naming any other backend refuses the failed local precondition,\n343|// never executes against the wrong backend.\n344|func checkLifecycleBackend(backendID string) error {\n345|\tif backendID != terminalbackend.BuiltinTmux {\n346|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"lifecycle backend\"}\n347|\t}\n348|\treturn nil\n349|}\n350|\n351|// checkBindingAgreement binds the create binding to its mutation\n352|// context: session, instance, backend, and generation must all agree.\n353|// Any disagreement refuses the failed local precondition: the binding\n354|// names another creation.\n355|func checkBindingAgreement(body CreateBody) error {\n356|\tif body.Binding.SessionID != body.Context.SessionID ||\n357|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalInstanceID != body.Context.TerminalInstanceID ||\n358|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalBackendID != body.Context.TerminalBackendID ||\n359|\t\tbody.Binding.BackendGeneration != body.Context.BackendGeneration {\n360|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"create binding agreement\"}\n361|\t}\n362|\treturn nil\n363|}\n364|\n365|// rowError normalizes a backend- or store-reported code against one\n366|// operation's allowed set: an in-row code propagates with its report,\n367|// while an outside-set code is itself refused as the protocol error —\n368|// the engine's CheckErrorAllowed arm, mirrored for the operations the\n369|// engine scope leaves out.\n370|func rowError(operation terminalbackend.Operation, err error) error {\n371|\tcode := backendErrorCode(err)\n372|\tif code == \"\" {\n373|\t\treturn err\n374|\t}\n375|\tif checkErr := terminalbackend.CheckErrorAllowed(string(operation), code); checkErr != nil {\n376|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"operation error vocabulary\"}\n377|\t}\n378|\treturn err\n379|}\n380|\n381|// formatTimestamp renders Now in the scalar timestamp grammar: UTC\n382|// RFC3339 with millisecond precision, always carrying the fractional\n383|// digits the grammar requires.\n384|func formatTimestamp(now time.Time) string {\n385|\treturn now.UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z07:00\")\n386|}\n387|\n388|// executeCreate runs the full create body: closed-shape admission,\n389|// backend and transport gates, binding agreement, then the landed\n390|// engine with the tmux backend. The result echoes the carried binding\n391|// and, exactly when interactive, the unbound attach descriptor.\n392|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeCreate(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n393|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate}\n394|\tbody, err := parseCreateBody(req.Body)\n395|\tif err != nil {\n396|\t\treturn empty, err\n397|\t}\n398|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.Context.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n399|\t\treturn empty, err\n400|\t}\n401|\tif body.Transport == string(terminalbackend.TransportThirdPartyRelay) {\n402|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized, Detail: \"create relay transport\"}\n403|\t}\n404|\tif err := checkBindingAgreement(body); err != nil {\n405|\t\treturn empty, err\n406|\t}\n407|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.Context.SessionID, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n408|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationCreate\n409|\treqBackend.bootstrapID = body.BootstrapOperationID\n410|\treqBackend.bindingID = body.Binding.BindingID\n411|\treqBackend.bindingDoc = append([]byte(nil), body.BindingRaw...)\n412|\t_, completedBefore, err := lc.Receipts.Completed(body.Context.IdempotencyKey)\n413|\tif err != nil {\n414|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeProcessFailed, Detail: \"idempotency store failure\"}\n415|\t}\n416|\tresult, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteMutating(ctx, terminalbackend.OperationCreate, body.Context, terminstance.Params{\n417|\t\tBootstrapOperationID: body.BootstrapOperationID,\n418|\t\tInteractive:          body.Interactive,\n419|\t}, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n420|\toutcome := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate, Binding: &body.Binding}\n421|\tif result.OperationID != \"\" {\n422|\t\toutcome.Mutation = &result\n423|\t\tif err != nil {\n424|\t\t\tlc.recordFailure(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n425|\t\t} else {\n426|\t\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n427|\t\t}\n428|\t}\n429|\tif err != nil {\n430|\t\treturn outcome, err\n431|\t}\n432|\tif !completedBefore {\n433|\t\t// A fresh create success opens a new incarnation: prior\n434|\t\t// closure reports are superseded, so the new\n435|\t\t// incarnation's input starts open. Replays skip the\n436|\t\t// rotation — replaying an old success must not erase a\n437|\t\t// newer closure — and a failed rotation fails the\n438|\t\t// operation closed: the incarnation keeps its prior\n439|\t\t// value, prior proofs stay valid, and recovery is a\n440|\t\t// fresh create or restore.\n441|\t\tif err := lc.States.RecordIncarnation(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, body.Context.IdempotencyKey); err != nil {\n442|\t\t\treturn outcome, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeIntegrityFailure, Detail: \"create incarnation image\"}\n443|\t\t}\n444|\t}\n445|\tif body.Interactive {\n446|\t\tdescriptor := createDescriptor(socket, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n447|\t\toutcome.Descriptor = &descriptor\n448|\t}\n449|\treturn outcome, nil\n450|}\n451|\n452|// executeStatus runs one status query through the landed engine with\n453|// the tmux backend: no receipt, no side effects, no authorization.\n454|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeStatus(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n455|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus}\n456|\tbody, err := terminstance.ParseStatusBody(req.Body)\n457|\tif err != nil {\n458|\t\treturn empty, err\n459|\t}\n460|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n461|\t\treturn empty, err\n462|\t}\n463|\tinstance := body.TerminalInstanceID\n464|\tif !body.HasTerminalInstanceID {\n465|\t\tinstance = \"\"\n466|\t}\n467|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.SessionID, instance)\n468|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationStatus\n469|\treport, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteStatus(ctx, body, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n470|\tif err != nil {\n471|\t\treturn empty, err\n472|\t}\n473|\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus, Status: &report}, nil\n474|}\n475|\n476|// executeEngineOp runs one quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, or\n477|// request-stop body through the landed engine with the tmux backend,\n478|// adding the per-operation success members the engine's receipt scope\n479|// leaves out.\n480|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeEngineOp(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string, operation terminalbackend.Operation) (OpOutcome, error) {\n481|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: operation}\n482|\tmctx, params, err := terminstance.ParseOperationBody(string(operation), req.Body)\n483|\tif err != nil {\n484|\t\treturn empty, err\n485|\t}\n486|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n487|\t\treturn empty, err\n488|\t}\n489|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n490|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n491|\tswitch operation {\n492|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n493|\t\treqBackend.quiescence = params.QuiescenceGeneration\n494|\t\treqBackend.channel = BoundaryChannelPrefix + params.QuiescenceGeneration\n495|\t\treqBackend.proofKind = params.ProviderProofKind\n496|\t\twaitCtx, cancel := lc.boundWait(ctx, mctx, params.TimeoutMs)\n497|\t\tdefer cancel()\n498|\t\treqBackend.waitCtx = waitCtx\n499|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n500|\t\t// The poll bound is the graceful wait: the lesser of the\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c75d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":521,"recorded_at":1780531400001037,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9a5-f59b-7f42-bddc-14e3de3b77d9"},"task_id":"01a0c9a5-f59b-7f42-bddc-14e3de3b77d9","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0c9a5-f59b-7f42-bddc-14e3de3b77d9"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c75f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":522,"recorded_at":1780531400001039,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"call_id":"call_01a0c9a5f18376d4ad65c5a1aaf07318","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/backend.go`.\n(499 line(s) above)\n500|\t}\n501|\tobserved, err := runner.runner.Run(ctx, confirm)\n502|\tif err != nil {\n503|\t\treturn \"\", errProbeUnknown\n504|\t}\n505|\tpresent, absent := classifyAbsence(observed, absentMarkerNoSession, absentMarkerNoSocket)\n506|\tif absent {\n507|\t\treturn effectEvidence(terminalbackend.EffectStaleIncarnationTerminated, runner.operation, runner.instanceID, \"confirmed-absent\"), nil\n508|\t}\n509|\tif !present {\n510|\t\treturn \"\", errProbeUnknown\n511|\t}\n512|\treturn \"\", &terminstance.Error{Code: terminstance.CodeProcessFailed, Detail: \"backend effect refused\"}\n513|}\n514|\n515|// command builds the argv for one directive over the request identity.\n516|func (runner *backend) command(directive Directive) ([]string, error) {\n517|\tbuilt, err := BuildCommand(directive, CommandArgs{\n518|\t\tRuntimeDir:           runner.runtimeDir,\n519|\t\tSocket:               runner.socket,\n520|\t\tSessionID:            runner.sessionID,\n521|\t\tInstanceID:           runner.instanceID,\n522|\t\tQuiescenceGeneration: runner.quiescence,\n523|\t})\n524|\tif err != nil {\n525|\t\tif code := backendErrorCode(err); code != \"\" {\n526|\t\t\treturn nil, &terminstance.Error{Code: code, Detail: \"backend command refused\"}\n527|\t\t}\n528|\t\treturn nil, err\n529|\t}\n530|\treturn built, nil\n531|}\n532|\n533|// backendErrorCode reads the wire code off a backend-construction or\n534|// store error: landed terminalbackend and terminstance refusals plus\n535|// local tmuxserver refusals all carry one. Anything else is uncoded.\n536|func backendErrorCode(err error) string {\n537|\tif code := terminstance.ErrorCode(err); code != \"\" {\n538|\t\treturn code\n539|\t}\n540|\tvar local *Error\n541|\tif errors.As(err, &local) {\n542|\t\treturn local.Code\n543|\t}\n544|\treturn \"\"\n545|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c761","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":523,"recorded_at":1780531400001041,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"call_id":"call_01a0c9a5f38973f8b0ade4d07defd89f","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/lifecycle.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"sync\"\n6|\t\"time\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/termbind\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n15|)\n16|\n17|// Lifecycle executes the eight tmux lifecycle operations — create,\n18|// attach, status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n19|// terminate-stale, restore — over the structured commands. Five\n20|// operations (create, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, request-stop,\n21|// status) delegate to the landed terminstance engine with the tmux\n22|// backend; attach, terminate-stale, and restore — which the engine\n23|// scope gate refuses — execute here over the same landed gates\n24|// (transition matrix, idempotency shapes, authorization, capability\n25|// conferral, receipt and binding stores) plus the tmux backend.\n26|//\n27|// A Lifecycle is constructed whole: every store and function value is\n28|// required (except Sleep/PollInterval, which default, and\n29|// ServerAdmission, which only attach needs). The Execute entry refuses\n30|// before any work when a dependency is missing.\n31|type Lifecycle struct {\n32|\t// RuntimeDir is the tmux runtime directory (<root>/tmux) the\n33|\t// socket derives from.\n34|\tRuntimeDir string\n35|\t// Root is the Runtime IPC root the socket custody verifies.\n36|\tRoot string\n37|\t// Platform selects the sun_path limit.\n38|\tPlatform scalar.Platform\n39|\t// Runner executes the tmux commands.\n40|\tRunner Runner\n41|\t// Receipts is the durable idempotency receipt table.\n42|\tReceipts *terminstance.ReceiptStore\n43|\t// Bindings is the durable bootstrap binding store.\n44|\tBindings *axpane.Store\n45|\t// Attach is the durable attach-client receipt store.\n46|\tAttach *termbind.AttachStore\n47|\t// States is the durable AX-side state memory.\n48|\tStates *InstanceStates\n49|\t// CurrentLease and CurrentGeneration re-read the winning lease\n50|\t// and the validated binding generation at every check point.\n51|\tCurrentLease      func() terminstance.LeaseView\n52|\tCurrentGeneration func() string\n53|\t// Now is the clock.\n54|\tNow func() time.Time\n55|\t// Sleep waits between close-confirm polls. Nil means time.Sleep.\n56|\tSleep func(time.Duration)\n57|\t// PollInterval separates close-confirm polls. Non-positive means\n58|\t// 50 milliseconds.\n59|\tPollInterval time.Duration\n60|\t// ServerAdmission reports the live server attestation the attach\n61|\t// handler binds to the request generation (the P3-A wiring: a\n62|\t// fresh decoy admission refuses here). Nil refuses attach only.\n63|\t// The context carries the operation deadline and the caller's\n64|\t// cancellation: a cooperative admission returns promptly when\n65|\t// it fires, and the attach entry additionally bounds the wait\n66|\t// itself, so even an adapter that ignores cancellation cannot\n67|\t// hold the request past its deadline or commit late.\n68|\tServerAdmission func(ctx context.Context) (RealmAdmission, error)\n69|\t// LocalHostID is the AX host identity the after-restore\n70|\t// composition compares the winning lease holder against. Empty\n71|\t// cannot prove a local win, so the composition parks or offers\n72|\t// remote attach only, never resumes.\n73|\tLocalHostID string\n74|\t// LeaseRefresh attempts the §4.2 mesh lease refresh\n75|\t// (after-restore step 2) under a timeout context. Nil skips the\n76|\t// attempt; a failed attempt also falls back to local knowledge.\n77|\t// Only a successful refresh verifies: the fallback decides\n78|\t// unverified, so it parks instead of resuming.\n79|\tLeaseRefresh func(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (RefreshWinner, error)\n80|\t// MeshRefreshTimeout bounds one refresh attempt. Non-positive\n81|\t// means DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout. The bound is enforced, not\n82|\t// advisory: the entry returns at the deadline even against an\n83|\t// adapter that ignores cancellation, and a late answer never\n84|\t// verifies.\n85|\tMeshRefreshTimeout time.Duration\n86|\t// Hooks observes receipts and effects. Nil disables observation.\n87|\tHooks *terminstance.EngineHooks\n88|\t// RefreshHooks arms the race boundary of the refresh select.\n89|\t// Nil in production.\n90|\tRefreshHooks *RefreshHooks\n91|\t// barrierMu serializes the input-closure ordering contract: the\n92|\t// quiesce report commit, the boundary report commit, and the\n93|\t// attach writable-receipt commit (barrier recheck, client\n94|\t// receipt, returned vector, advisory memory) are mutually\n95|\t// exclusive, so whichever lands first wins and no writable\n96|\t// receipt commits after a durable closure report. The initial\n97|\t// attach fast-path check and the server admission run outside\n98|\t// the lock (admission may block); only the recheck-to-vector\n99|\t// section holds it. The quiesce engine closure runs inside the\n100|\t// lock (its tmux effects return immediately); the boundary wait\n101|\t// runs outside (it blocks on the wrapper signal) and only its\n102|\t// report commit takes the lock. Non-reentrant: hooks firing\n103|\t// inside a locked section must not call Execute. The contract\n104|\t// is in-process: concurrent ax processes racing attach against\n105|\t// quiesce serialize only through the report files, not through\n106|\t// this mutex (bound B42). The vector handoff the contract\n107|\t// covers ends at vector construction: a caller that execs a\n108|\t// pre-quiescence vector after quiescence commits holds a\n109|\t// pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\n110|\tbarrierMu sync.Mutex\n111|}\n112|\n113|// RefreshHooks arms the race boundary of the mesh lease refresh:\n114|// BeforeSelect runs after the adapter launches and before the entry\n115|// selects over the answer and the deadline. A nil hook is a no-op.\n116|// Tests stall past the bound to force the both-ready race\n117|// deterministically: without the stall the deadline arm always wins\n118|// and the answer-path expiry check never triggers.\n119|type RefreshHooks struct {\n120|\tBeforeSelect func()\n121|}\n122|\n123|// DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout bounds the after-restore mesh lease\n124|// refresh when the Lifecycle leaves it unset: five seconds, after\n125|// which the branch proceeds on local knowledge instead of blocking\n126|// forever.\n127|const DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout = 5 * time.Second\n128|\n129|// RefreshWinner is one mesh lease-refresh answer: the winning lease\n130|// tuple and its holder host.\n131|type RefreshWinner struct {\n132|\tLeaseID      string\n133|\tEpoch        uint64\n134|\tHolderHostID string\n135|}\n136|\n137|// OpRequest is one lifecycle operation request: the operation name,\n138|// its closed body, the presented source state, the admitted\n139|// capabilities, and the fencing material (for terminate-stale only).\n140|type OpRequest struct {\n141|\tOperation            string\n142|\tBody                 []byte\n143|\tSource               string\n144|\tAdmitted             terminalbackend.Admitted\n145|\tPresented            fencing.PresentedToken\n146|\tWinner               sessrepo.LeaseSummary\n147|\tHasWinner            bool\n148|\tForceRecovery        bool\n149|\tDiagnosticsPreserved bool\n150|}\n151|\n152|// AttachOutcome is the attach success payload: the client mirror, the\n153|// host-local descriptor, the authorized input boolean, and the\n154|// evidence. The result input boolean always equals the request and the\n155|// authorization; the landed CheckAttachResult proves it on every call.\n156|type AttachOutcome struct {\n157|\tClientMirrorID  string\n158|\tDescriptor      string\n159|\tInputAuthorized bool\n160|\tEvidenceIDs     []string\n161|}\n162|\n163|// OpOutcome is one executed operation: exactly one of Mutation,\n164|// Status, or Attach is set, plus the per-operation success members.\n165|// Mutation is set on every executed mutating path — success and\n166|// coded failure alike, mirroring the engine — and nil only when the\n167|// request was malformed before any result existed.\n168|type OpOutcome struct {\n169|\tOperation              terminalbackend.Operation\n170|\tMutation               *terminstance.Result\n171|\tStatus                 *terminstance.StatusReport\n172|\tAttach                 *AttachOutcome\n173|\tArgv                   []string\n174|\tBinding                *termbind.Binding\n175|\tDescriptor             *string\n176|\tPriorBindingID         string\n177|\tRestoredParked         bool\n178|\tTargetClosed           bool\n179|\tProcessClosed          bool\n180|\tStoreClosed            bool\n181|\tQuiescenceGeneration   string\n182|\tInputClosedAt          string\n183|\tSafeBoundaryEvidenceID string\n184|\tBoundaryObservedAt     string\n185|}\n186|\n187|// Execute runs one lifecycle operation to its outcome. Refusals\n188|// precede side effects: malformed operations, unknown backends, and\n189|// unsafe sockets refuse before any store or tmux interaction. The\n190|// socket custody (before-connect rejection) and length refusal run on\n191|// every operation, because every operation connects.\n192|func (lc *Lifecycle) Execute(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest) (OpOutcome, error) {\n193|\tempty := OpOutcome{}\n194|\tif lc == nil || lc.Runner == nil || lc.Receipts == nil || lc.Bindings == nil ||\n195|\t\tlc.Attach == nil || lc.States == nil ||\n196|\t\tlc.CurrentLease == nil || lc.CurrentGeneration == nil || lc.Now == nil {\n197|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle dependencies\"}\n198|\t}\n199|\toperation, err := terminalbackend.ParseOperation(req.Operation)\n200|\tif err != nil {\n201|\t\treturn empty, err\n202|\t}\n203|\tif _, err := DirectivesFor(operation); err != nil {\n204|\t\treturn empty, err\n205|\t}\n206|\tsocket := SocketPath(lc.RuntimeDir)\n207|\tif err := CheckSocketLength(socket, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n208|\t\treturn empty, err\n209|\t}\n210|\tif err := CheckSocketCustody(socket, lc.Root, lc.Platform); err != nil {\n211|\t\treturn empty, err\n212|\t}\n213|\tswitch operation {\n214|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationCreate:\n215|\t\treturn lc.executeCreate(ctx, req, socket)\n216|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationAttach:\n217|\t\treturn lc.executeAttach(ctx, req, socket)\n218|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationStatus:\n219|\t\treturn lc.executeStatus(ctx, req, socket)\n220|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\n221|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n222|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n223|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n224|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n225|\t\treturn lc.executeEngineOp(ctx, req, socket, operation)\n226|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationTerminateStale:\n227|\t\treturn lc.executeTerminate(ctx, req, socket)\n228|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRestore:\n229|\t\treturn lc.executeRestore(ctx, req, socket)\n230|\tdefault:\n231|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle operation\"}\n232|\t}\n233|}\n234|\n235|// engineFor builds the per-call landed engine over a request-scoped\n236|// tmux backend. The engine is a plain struct: constructing one per\n237|// call keeps request identity out of shared state.\n238|func (lc *Lifecycle) engineFor(reqBackend *backend) *terminstance.Engine {\n239|\treturn &terminstance.Engine{\n240|\t\tStore:             lc.Receipts,\n241|\t\tBackend:           reqBackend,\n242|\t\tCurrentLease:      lc.CurrentLease,\n243|\t\tCurrentGeneration: lc.CurrentGeneration,\n244|\t\tNow:               lc.Now,\n245|\t\tHooks:             lc.Hooks,\n246|\t}\n247|}\n248|\n249|// requestBackend builds the request-scoped tmux backend over the\n250|// lifecycle stores and the admitted set.\n251|func (lc *Lifecycle) requestBackend(req OpRequest, socket, session, instance string) *backend {\n252|\tsleep := lc.Sleep\n253|\tif sleep == nil {\n254|\t\tsleep = time.Sleep\n255|\t}\n256|\tpoll := lc.PollInterval\n257|\tif poll <= 0 {\n258|\t\tpoll = 50 * time.Millisecond\n259|\t}\n260|\treturn &backend{\n261|\t\trunner:     lc.Runner,\n262|\t\truntimeDir: lc.RuntimeDir,\n263|\t\tsocket:     socket,\n264|\t\tsessionID:  session,\n265|\t\tinstanceID: instance,\n266|\t\tnow:        lc.Now,\n267|\t\tsleep:      sleep,\n268|\t\tpoll:       poll,\n269|\t\tadmitted:   req.Admitted,\n270|\t\tbindings:   lc.Bindings,\n271|\t\tattach:     lc.Attach,\n272|\t\tstates:     lc.States,\n273|\t\tkillExit:   -1,\n274|\t}\n275|}\n276|\n277|// recordAfter records the adopted after-state in the AX-side memory on\n278|// success paths. The memory is advisory everywhere: status\n279|// reconciles the live probe against it, but attach admission never\n280|// consults it — only the incarnation-scoped closure proof decides\n281|// admission, so a stale or lost memory record can neither reopen a\n282|// closed barrier nor close an open one. On the barrier successes\n283|// (quiesce-input and wait-safe-boundary) the caller still checks the\n284|// returned error and fails closed, keeping the status memory\n285|// faithful to the closure the operation just proved.\n286|func (lc *Lifecycle) recordAfter(instance string, after terminalbackend.InstanceState) error {\n287|\tif lc.States == nil {\n288|\t\treturn nil\n289|\t}\n290|\treturn lc.States.Record(instance, after)\n291|}\n292|\n293|// recordFailure records the after-state of a failed operation. A\n294|// failure with committed effects and an uncertain tail (After\n295|// unavailable) overwrites with the honest unknown: the prior record\n296|// no longer describes the instance. A pure refusal proves nothing —\n297|// its After echoes the caller-carried source — so it installs that\n298|// echo only when the memory holds no record at all (letting the\n299|// uncertain-resume path reconcile a first-operation failure) and\n300|// never overwrites an authoritative record with stale caller state.\n301|// Failure reporting can never reopen a closed barrier: attach\n302|// admission never consults this memory, and a refusal either\n303|// preserves the prior record, installs a first echo, or records the\n304|// non-admitting unknown.\n305|func (lc *Lifecycle) recordFailure(instance string, after terminalbackend.InstanceState) {\n306|\tif lc.States == nil {\n307|\t\treturn\n308|\t}\n309|\tif after == terminalbackend.StateUnavailable {\n310|\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(instance, after)\n311|\t\treturn\n312|\t}\n313|\t_, found, err := lc.States.Lookup(instance)\n314|\tif err != nil || found {\n315|\t\treturn\n316|\t}\n317|\t_ = lc.recordAfter(instance, after)\n318|}\n319|\n320|// mutationResult assembles a lifecycle result with the engine's\n321|// buildResult contract: repeated request identities, before/after\n322|// states, bytewise-sorted effects and evidence, and one disposition.\n323|func mutationResult(mctx terminstance.MutationContext, before, after terminalbackend.InstanceState, effects []terminalbackend.SideEffect, evidence []string, disposition terminstance.RetryDisposition) terminstance.Result {\n324|\treturn terminstance.Result{\n325|\t\tOperationID:           mctx.OperationID,\n326|\t\tSessionID:             mctx.SessionID,\n327|\t\tTerminalInstanceID:    mctx.TerminalInstanceID,\n328|\t\tTerminalBackendID:     mctx.TerminalBackendID,\n329|\t\tImplementationVersion: mctx.ImplementationVersion,\n330|\t\tProtocolVersion:       mctx.ProtocolVersion,\n331|\t\tBackendGeneration:     mctx.BackendGeneration,\n332|\t\tBefore:                before,\n333|\t\tAfter:                 after,\n334|\t\tEffects:               sortedEffects(effects),\n335|\t\tEvidenceIDs:           sortedEvidence(evidence),\n336|\t\tDisposition:           disposition,\n337|\t}\n338|}\n339|\n340|// checkLifecycleBackend admits exactly the tmux backend identity: this\n341|// lifecycle executes for ax.tmux and no other backend. A request\n342|// naming any other backend refuses the failed local precondition,\n343|// never executes against the wrong backend.\n344|func checkLifecycleBackend(backendID string) error {\n345|\tif backendID != terminalbackend.BuiltinTmux {\n346|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"lifecycle backend\"}\n347|\t}\n348|\treturn nil\n349|}\n350|\n351|// checkBindingAgreement binds the create binding to its mutation\n352|// context: session, instance, backend, and generation must all agree.\n353|// Any disagreement refuses the failed local precondition: the binding\n354|// names another creation.\n355|func checkBindingAgreement(body CreateBody) error {\n356|\tif body.Binding.SessionID != body.Context.SessionID ||\n357|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalInstanceID != body.Context.TerminalInstanceID ||\n358|\t\tbody.Binding.TerminalBackendID != body.Context.TerminalBackendID ||\n359|\t\tbody.Binding.BackendGeneration != body.Context.BackendGeneration {\n360|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"create binding agreement\"}\n361|\t}\n362|\treturn nil\n363|}\n364|\n365|// rowError normalizes a backend- or store-reported code against one\n366|// operation's allowed set: an in-row code propagates with its report,\n367|// while an outside-set code is itself refused as the protocol error —\n368|// the engine's CheckErrorAllowed arm, mirrored for the operations the\n369|// engine scope leaves out.\n370|func rowError(operation terminalbackend.Operation, err error) error {\n371|\tcode := backendErrorCode(err)\n372|\tif code == \"\" {\n373|\t\treturn err\n374|\t}\n375|\tif checkErr := terminalbackend.CheckErrorAllowed(string(operation), code); checkErr != nil {\n376|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"operation error vocabulary\"}\n377|\t}\n378|\treturn err\n379|}\n380|\n381|// formatTimestamp renders Now in the scalar timestamp grammar: UTC\n382|// RFC3339 with millisecond precision, always carrying the fractional\n383|// digits the grammar requires.\n384|func formatTimestamp(now time.Time) string {\n385|\treturn now.UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z07:00\")\n386|}\n387|\n388|// executeCreate runs the full create body: closed-shape admission,\n389|// backend and transport gates, binding agreement, then the landed\n390|// engine with the tmux backend. The result echoes the carried binding\n391|// and, exactly when interactive, the unbound attach descriptor.\n392|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeCreate(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n393|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate}\n394|\tbody, err := parseCreateBody(req.Body)\n395|\tif err != nil {\n396|\t\treturn empty, err\n397|\t}\n398|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.Context.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n399|\t\treturn empty, err\n400|\t}\n401|\tif body.Transport == string(terminalbackend.TransportThirdPartyRelay) {\n402|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized, Detail: \"create relay transport\"}\n403|\t}\n404|\tif err := checkBindingAgreement(body); err != nil {\n405|\t\treturn empty, err\n406|\t}\n407|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.Context.SessionID, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n408|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationCreate\n409|\treqBackend.bootstrapID = body.BootstrapOperationID\n410|\treqBackend.bindingID = body.Binding.BindingID\n411|\treqBackend.bindingDoc = append([]byte(nil), body.BindingRaw...)\n412|\t_, completedBefore, err := lc.Receipts.Completed(body.Context.IdempotencyKey)\n413|\tif err != nil {\n414|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminstance.CodeProcessFailed, Detail: \"idempotency store failure\"}\n415|\t}\n416|\tresult, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteMutating(ctx, terminalbackend.OperationCreate, body.Context, terminstance.Params{\n417|\t\tBootstrapOperationID: body.BootstrapOperationID,\n418|\t\tInteractive:          body.Interactive,\n419|\t}, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n420|\toutcome := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationCreate, Binding: &body.Binding}\n421|\tif result.OperationID != \"\" {\n422|\t\toutcome.Mutation = &result\n423|\t\tif err != nil {\n424|\t\t\tlc.recordFailure(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n425|\t\t} else {\n426|\t\t\t_ = lc.recordAfter(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, result.After)\n427|\t\t}\n428|\t}\n429|\tif err != nil {\n430|\t\treturn outcome, err\n431|\t}\n432|\tif !completedBefore {\n433|\t\t// A fresh create success opens a new incarnation: prior\n434|\t\t// closure reports are superseded, so the new\n435|\t\t// incarnation's input starts open. Replays skip the\n436|\t\t// rotation — replaying an old success must not erase a\n437|\t\t// newer closure — and a failed rotation fails the\n438|\t\t// operation closed: the incarnation keeps its prior\n439|\t\t// value, prior proofs stay valid, and recovery is a\n440|\t\t// fresh create or restore.\n441|\t\tif err := lc.States.RecordIncarnation(body.Context.TerminalInstanceID, body.Context.IdempotencyKey); err != nil {\n442|\t\t\treturn outcome, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeIntegrityFailure, Detail: \"create incarnation image\"}\n443|\t\t}\n444|\t}\n445|\tif body.Interactive {\n446|\t\tdescriptor := createDescriptor(socket, body.Context.TerminalInstanceID)\n447|\t\toutcome.Descriptor = &descriptor\n448|\t}\n449|\treturn outcome, nil\n450|}\n451|\n452|// executeStatus runs one status query through the landed engine with\n453|// the tmux backend: no receipt, no side effects, no authorization.\n454|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeStatus(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string) (OpOutcome, error) {\n455|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus}\n456|\tbody, err := terminstance.ParseStatusBody(req.Body)\n457|\tif err != nil {\n458|\t\treturn empty, err\n459|\t}\n460|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(body.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n461|\t\treturn empty, err\n462|\t}\n463|\tinstance := body.TerminalInstanceID\n464|\tif !body.HasTerminalInstanceID {\n465|\t\tinstance = \"\"\n466|\t}\n467|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, body.SessionID, instance)\n468|\treqBackend.operation = terminalbackend.OperationStatus\n469|\treport, err := lc.engineFor(reqBackend).ExecuteStatus(ctx, body, terminalbackend.InstanceState(req.Source), req.Admitted)\n470|\tif err != nil {\n471|\t\treturn empty, err\n472|\t}\n473|\treturn OpOutcome{Operation: terminalbackend.OperationStatus, Status: &report}, nil\n474|}\n475|\n476|// executeEngineOp runs one quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary, or\n477|// request-stop body through the landed engine with the tmux backend,\n478|// adding the per-operation success members the engine's receipt scope\n479|// leaves out.\n480|func (lc *Lifecycle) executeEngineOp(ctx context.Context, req OpRequest, socket string, operation terminalbackend.Operation) (OpOutcome, error) {\n481|\tempty := OpOutcome{Operation: operation}\n482|\tmctx, params, err := terminstance.ParseOperationBody(string(operation), req.Body)\n483|\tif err != nil {\n484|\t\treturn empty, err\n485|\t}\n486|\tif err := checkLifecycleBackend(mctx.TerminalBackendID); err != nil {\n487|\t\treturn empty, err\n488|\t}\n489|\treqBackend := lc.requestBackend(req, socket, mctx.SessionID, mctx.TerminalInstanceID)\n490|\treqBackend.operation = operation\n491|\tswitch operation {\n492|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\n493|\t\treqBackend.quiescence = params.QuiescenceGeneration\n494|\t\treqBackend.channel = BoundaryChannelPrefix + params.QuiescenceGeneration\n495|\t\treqBackend.proofKind = params.ProviderProofKind\n496|\t\twaitCtx, cancel := lc.boundWait(ctx, mctx, params.TimeoutMs)\n497|\t\tdefer cancel()\n498|\t\treqBackend.waitCtx = waitCtx\n499|\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\n500|\t\t// The poll bound is the graceful wait: the lesser of the\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
