{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb15","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":997,"recorded_at":1780531400001989,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9ae-1050-7f10-a012-d1b5860e00c3"},"task_id":"01a0c9ae-1050-7f10-a012-d1b5860e00c3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9ae-1050-7f10-a012-d1b5860e00c3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(579 line(s) above)\n580|PRB 1 / SPW 1 shared; backendid 6 EX shared 1; agreement EXC 4\n581|members; enginemembers EXE 4 members; attachcap EXA 2 members;\n582|attestation EXA 1 + pinned member; attachdeadline EXA 2 arms;\n583|authkind EXT 2 / EXR 2 (entry 1 / shared loop 1 each; D-loop wiring\n584|supplementary, uncounted); generation EXA 1 / EXT 1 / EXR 2; deadline\n585|EXA 2 / EXT 1 / EXR 2; keymaterial EXT 1 / EXR\n586|1; capdual EXT 2 members; fencingmap EXT 2 + 3 pinned; target EXT 3\n587|members; winner EXT 2 members (session arm U3: fencing+target\n588|precede); record EXT 1 / EXR 1 shared + UNT 1; replay EXT 2 + 6\n589|pinned; bindmap/bindfound single-sided at EXT; readonly EXA 1 / CMD 1\n590|shared; detachvec CMD 1; boundarykind/boundexit EXE 1 each + PFX\n591|0/1; quiescedetach EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; nosendkeys/closeexit EXE 1\n592|each; probemarker EXS 1 / EXE 1 / EXT 1 shared; probeneg EXE 1;\n593|identity CUS 1; bindcontract/restoreagree EXR 1 each; replaytime EXE\n594|2; after-restore outcomes in Table E (launch/reattach/offer/park/\n595|refuse + refresh audit); outcomekey REC 1 / LOOK 1; binddocid REC\n596|1 / LOOK 1; binddocshape REC 1; docpersist EXR 1; attachreadonly\n597|EXA 1; quiescereport/boundaryreport EXE 3 rows each\n598|(corrupt/empty/crash legs); statusunbound/statusdoc/statusmatch/\n599|statusnegative EXS 1 each + statusmatch LOOK 1; prioragree EXR 4\n600|tests, 3 rows; succession EXR 3 members; execdeps 6 EX pinned\n601|(B36); Table B verify 9 new-entry sides shared 1, server EXA 1 (its\n602|other sides are first-leaf symmetry). Revision-4 gates:\n603|quiescerecord/boundaryrecord single-sided at EXE;\n604|barrierquiesce/barrierboundary/barrierdecode/barrierempty\n605|single-sided at EXA (same entry as the quiescegate memory arm, whose\n606|row points at them); attachedexit/foreignrow/panesexit single\n607|measured side at EXS (EXT/EXR B39 via the resume reconcile);\n608|argvnul single-sided at OSR (mirrors osrun: no committed Execute\n609|composition injects OSRunner). Revision-5 gates:\n610|barrierincarnation/barrierkey/attachhealth single-sided at EXA;\n611|failurerecord EXE 1 / UNT 1 (different arms: never-overwrite vs\n612|call value); createincarnation EXC 2 rows; restoreincarnation EXR\n613|1 + structural D row / EXT 1; incarnationrecord REC 2 members;\n614|incarnationlookup LOOK 3 members. Rotation symmetry:\n615|createincarnation EXC 1 narrowing row / restoreincarnation EXR 1\n616|narrowing row (symmetric); rootwrite gains PRB 1 (CUS 1 / EXC 1 /\n617|EXS 1 / EXR 1 / PRB 1 / SPW 1 / shared EachOperation row);\n618|statelookup gains EXA 1 alongside LOOK 2 (different arms: absent\n619|vs grammar); statusnegative EXS 2 rows (negative + parse legs).\n620|Revision-6 gates: recheck single-sided at EXA; ordering EXA 1 /\n621|EXE 2 with the three-sided symmetry attach 1 / quiesce 1 /\n622|boundary 1; barrierread EXA 2 arms with the symmetry\n623|directory-read 1 / file-read 1; incarnationlookup gains EXA 1\n624|alongside LOOK 3 (different arms: read-error vs grammar);\n625|rootwrite EXA gains the entry row alongside the shared row (the\n626|valid-body attach is served when the gate is weakened for attach\n627|alone). Revision-8 gates: effectrecheck single-column at EXE with\n628|the two-site symmetry stop 4 / quiesce 4 (3 shared arms + 1\n629|per-site skip row each); overlapmulti/overlapinput single-sided at\n630|EXA; waitbound EXA 1 / EXE 1 shared (4 killers across\n631|attach-admission, attach-barrier, quiesce-span, and\n632|boundary-commit; the cancellation companion stays green);\n633|attachdeadline/deadline EXA gain the shared wait row beside the\n634|survived-supplementary entry row.\n635|\n636|Ratio: 261 measured of 5376 (50+10+201 M across Tables A/B/D;\n637|Table C all U); 187 bound; 4928 unreachable with reasons. Every\n638|driven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 28\n639|driven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\n640|B29 poll past-deadline, B32 propagation, B36 singleton deps) and\n641|155 named undriven gaps (B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch\n642|side, and the 147 B39 reachable-undriven cells), each with its\n643|owner below; B40/B41/B42/B43/B44 are non-cell bounds stated below.\n644|(Table A's 4 B15 guard-name arms are bound outside this split.)\n645|\n646|Table E: after-restore outcome grid (ExecuteWrapperRestore,\n647|wrapper.go:97). Each row is one decided outcome with its evidence\n648|condition, its backend effect, and the committed test plus the\n649|narrowing row that kills a routing/order mutant through the\n650|wrapper entry (test names drop the Test prefix):\n651|\n652|| Outcome | Evidence condition | Backend effect | Test / row |\n653||---|---|---|---|\n654|| launch | verified local win + valid materialization | executes backend restore exactly once | WrapperRestoreLocalWinResumes; reorder covered by N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n655|| reattach | verified local win + recorded bootstrap pair | executes backend restore exactly once | WrapperRestoreReattachReplaysBackend; reorder covered by N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n656|| attach_remote | refreshed remote winner + lapsed local grant + interactive | none (no backend op, no exec, no provider) | WrapperRestoreLapsedGrantRemoteOffer/attach; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n657|| takeover_offer | refreshed remote winner + lapsed local grant + non-capable attach | none (no backend op, no exec, no provider) | WrapperRestoreLapsedGrantRemoteOffer/takeover; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n658|| parked (remote-noninteractive) | refreshed remote winner + non-interactive terminal | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/remote-noninteractive; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n659|| parked (refresh-failed) | refresh error → unverified local knowledge | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/refresh-failed; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n660|| parked (no-adapter) | missing refresh adapter → unverified local knowledge | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/no-adapter; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n661|| parked (no-known-lease) | no lease known at all → zero winner | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/no-known-lease; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n662|| parked (invalid-material) | required materialization not admitted | none (routing mutant would execute) | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/invalid-material; N-wrapper-route-material |\n663|| parked (refresh-timeout) | refresh blocks → cancelled at the bound, unverified | none | WrapperRestoreRefreshBoundMeasured/configured-50ms; N-refresh-bound-default (default leg) |\n664|| parked (expired refresh) | refresh answers after the deadline with a nil error → rejected, unverified | none | WrapperRestoreExpiredRefreshParksUnverified; expiry covered by N-wrapper-refresh-expired |\n665|| parked (late-answer race) | both-ready selection → the late answer never verifies | none | WrapperRestoreRefreshRaceRejectsLateAnswer; N-wrapper-refresh-expired |\n666|| parked (non-cooperative adapter) | adapter ignores cancellation → the entry returns at the bound | none | WrapperRestoreRefreshBoundEnforced; N-wrapper-refresh-deadline |\n667|| refuse (divergent winner) | refreshed winner ≠ carried restore authorization | none, failed local precondition | WrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentWinner(+Lease,+Epoch); N-wrapper-winner-lease, N-wrapper-winner-epoch |\n668|| refuse (divergent session) | decision session ≠ restore session | none, failed local precondition | WrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentSession; N-wrapper-restore-session |\n669|| refuse (divergent bootstrap) | decision bootstrap ≠ restore bootstrap | none, failed local precondition | ReviewWrapperBootstrapMustBindExecutedRestore; N-wrapper-restore-bootstrap |\n670|| refuse (divergent instance) | admitted descriptor instance ≠ restore instance | none, failed local precondition | ReviewWrapperInstanceMustBindExecutedRestore; N-wrapper-restore-instance |\n671|| refuse (divergent backend) | admitted descriptor backend ≠ restore backend | none, failed local precondition | WrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentBackend; N-wrapper-restore-backend |\n672|| refuse (divergent generation) | admitted descriptor generation ≠ restore generation | none, failed local precondition | WrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentGeneration; N-wrapper-restore-generation |\n673|| refuse (mode) | Decide.Mode != restore (incl. garbage) | none, invalid-arguments | WrapperRestoreRefusesMalformed; N-wrapper-mode |\n674|| refuse (operation) | Restore.Operation != restore (incl. garbage) | none, invalid-arguments | WrapperRestoreRefusesMalformed; N-wrapper-operation |\n675|| refuse (deps) | nil lifecycle or nil dependency | none, protocol-error | WrapperRestoreRefusesMalformed; B36 singleton (no narrowing row) |\n676|\n677|The refresh runs before the decision on every row (N-wrapper-\n678|reorder-refresh admits exactly the fixture session past the\n679|refresh-success arm into stale local knowledge and is killed by\n680|the offer/resume/park tests together), so the offer path never\n681|presents the lapsed grant to backend restore authorization. The\n682|resume rows execute only bound to the decided session, bootstrap,\n683|instance, backend, generation, and winner as one composed\n684|authorization (N-wrapper-restore-session, N-wrapper-restore-\n685|bootstrap, N-wrapper-restore-instance, N-wrapper-restore-backend,\n686|N-wrapper-restore-generation, N-wrapper-winner-lease,\n687|N-wrapper-winner-epoch); late answers never verify whether they\n688|arrive after the deadline (N-wrapper-refresh-expired) or the\n689|adapter ignores cancellation (N-wrapper-refresh-deadline). No\n690|production mesh transport backs the adapter (B37). Union-rival\n691|ambiguity is unmodeled (B38). The parked wire result\n692|of the backend restore entry itself (RestoredParked) stays a\n693|backend-row concern, not a Table E row.\n694|\n695|## Stated bounds\n696|\n697|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n698|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n699|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n700|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n701|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n702|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n703|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n704|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n705|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n706|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n707|  panic kill.\n708|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n709|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n710|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n711|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n712|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n713|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n714|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n715|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n716|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n717|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n718|  conformance matrix only.\n719|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n720|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n721|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n722|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n723|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n724|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n725|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n726|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n727|  Dependencies.Spawn is inert on the background path: a nil spawner\n728|  with a live broker still contacts (the broker path never calls it),\n729|  so the field is dead weight there — which is what makes the\n730|  shared-Dependencies fallback shape realistic, and why the spy\n731|  census arms the foreground probe alongside the spawner.\n732|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n733|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n734|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n735|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n736|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n737|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n738|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n739|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n740|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir\n741|  (witnessed by TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape); through Acquire\n742|  the directory always names a created directory.\n743|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n744|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n745|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n746|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n747|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n748|- B14 The battery and the read-only-root test assume a non-root test\n749|  user: N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit\n750|  chmod, so under root it is equivalent to the original and survives,\n751|  and TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot stages a genuine EACCES\n752|  only when permission bits bind the test user. The reviewer's\n753|  same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.\n754|- B15 Unmeasured fail-closed stat arms, no seam: handleBoundToPath's\n755|  two stat-failure arms (runtime.go) and verifyOwnership's !ok arm\n756|  (ownership_unix.go) fail closed by code and are prose only by test —\n757|  no test can stage a Stat failure on an open directory handle, or a\n758|  stat without ownership metadata on unix, without a seam. The\n759|  guard.Resolve refusal arm (runtime.go) is unreachable through the\n760|  name grammar: every input the guard would refuse is refused earlier\n761|  by scalar, so the fail-open plant survives by construction. The\n762|  secprim.NewGuard refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) is the same class:\n763|  no committed input reaches it. The same unstageable class covers\n764|  the commit-side Fchmod and parent-Fsync failure arms and the\n765|  commit-side (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and verify-side leaf-Stat\n766|  failure arms: no committed test stages those failures. An\n767|  unopenable (0000) root reports `runtime containment` on both entries\n768|  with no committed test staging it — classifying EACCES as missing\n769|  would reroute it to `runtime root`, refusal-to-refusal. Reported\n770|  as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n771|- B16 The collision gate compares cleaned byte strings: an ambient\n772|  value naming the derived socket through a symlinked or relative\n773|  alias of the root walks past it 