{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb3f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":1018,"recorded_at":1780531400002031,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9ae-2576-76a2-ae7e-788995ea78d4"},"task_id":"01a0c9ae-2576-76a2-ae7e-788995ea78d4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9ae-2576-76a2-ae7e-788995ea78d4","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(779 line(s) above)\n780|  package-local defense-in-depth claim. An `ax` invocation from\n781|  inside its own AX pane refuses `ambient collision` when the caller\n782|  populates Ambient from the process environment\n783|  (TMUX=`<derived>`,pid,idx in the real encoding): over-strict\n784|  rather than over-permissive, and the caller owns what it observes\n785|  — the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz decides the\n786|  nested-invocation rule deliberately.\n787|- B17 The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on\n788|  a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This\n789|  matches the landed hosttrust custody precedent\n790|  (internal/hosttrust/custody_unix.go platformModeOK: Perm() == mode),\n791|  so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n792|- B18 The derived socket path is not checked against the platform\n793|  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep runtime root surfaces\n794|  as a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter, owned by\n795|  TASK-260830-1c28dz.\n796|- B19 The Runtime IPC root's own mode and ownership are not gated in\n797|  this leaf: the root arrives as the caller-supplied\n798|  localstore-resolved PathRuntime value, its creation-time custody is\n799|  the localstore layout owner's, and the SPEC 810-812\n800|  before-bind/connect rejection of an unsafe path, parent, or ancestor\n801|  is the lifecycle bind step's (TASK-260830-1c28dz), which is the step\n802|  that binds. This leaf pins the root handle (no-follow open plus\n803|  handle/path binding) and commits the leaf relative to it; a\n804|  world-writable root is admitted here and refused at bind. That the\n805|  root value is the landed localstore PathRuntime is a contract\n806|  statement about the caller, not a driven fact: no test composes\n807|  localstore with Acquire.\n808|- B20 Whether the runtime leaf was created by AX is indistinguishable\n809|  after the fact: any same-user 0700 directory under an admitted name\n810|  is accepted. The verifiable properties — mode, ownership, kind,\n811|  containment — are gated (rows 1-15); provenance is not claimed.\n812|- B21 No broker is modelled as the zero BrokerReport, whose\n813|  Principal.UID is 0: for a non-root process the absent broker\n814|  refuses on the authentication arm, while under a root process the\n815|  same-user arm passes and refusal comes from the generation arm.\n816|  The broker-path outcome socket binding is the generation equality\n817|  only — BrokerReport carries no socket of its own.\n818|- B22 Singleton arms ship no narrowing mutant: admitting the\n819|  singleton refused member is deleting the gate. Covered sites, each\n820|  test-pinned in both directions where a fork exists: create relay\n821|  transport (relay), descriptor presence fork (descpresence),\n822|  attach admission nil (serveadmitnil), spawner runner nil\n823|  (spawnnil), reconcile verifier nil (reconcilenil), states root\n824|  empty (stateopen), persist/attach stores nil (storenil),\n825|  failed-kill self-confirm (selfconfirm), live-after-escalation\n826|  (stoptimeout), and post-wait boundaries without a configured\n827|  revalidation (recheckPostWait nil). The outcome-lookup empty-key\n828|  arm left this bound: it narrows now (LookupOutcomeRefusesForgedKey /\n829|  N-outcome-key-forged). Owner: this leaf; retest if any site\n830|  grows a second refused member.\n831|- B23 The landed status engine normalizes backend error details to\n832|  \"status observation unknown\" (coded or not), so the cutrow and\n833|  empty-panes narrowings measure at the helper entries while the\n834|  dispatch legs pin the code. Owner: this leaf; retest if the\n835|  engine stops normalizing.\n836|- B24 The idempotency-store Completed read-failure arm is unstaged:\n837|  no seam fails receipt reads (hooks fire on write paths only).\n838|  Owner: hardening; stage with a read-failure seam to measure.\n839|- B25 The Bind clean-miss sub-arm is unstageable: every Bind error\n840|  the hooks stage leaves the committed file, so Lookup always finds\n841|  it. The clean-found sub-arm is measured (N-bind-hook-found).\n842|  Owner: hardening.\n843|- B26 The attach effect-failure dispatch mapping is unstaged: no\n844|  committed failure reaches it (the store replays identical\n845|  receipts; conflicting receipts are untested at dispatch).\n846|  Owner: hardening.\n847|- B27 No committed test composes the Production Dependencies into\n848|  Acquire: AFG reaches the adapter and bind gates only through\n849|  caller-injected implementations (the 18 Table C U2c cells). The\n850|  injection seam is first-leaf-owned; Production wiring is\n851|  unit-pinned (TestProductionWiresDependencies). Owner: composition\n852|  test, sibling scope.\n853|- B28 The backend command-error wrap is unmeasured at PFX (no\n854|  backend test stages a refused build; the builder rows pin the\n855|  refused shapes at CMD). Owner: this leaf; retest with a\n856|  refused-build backend test.\n857|- B29 The close-confirm poll deadline is pinned for past-deadline\n858|  at PFX via direct staging; the exact-boundary member and\n859|  dispatch-level staging are unmeasured (the fake runner advances\n860|  no time). Owner: hardening.\n861|- B30 The OSRunner exit/transport/argv mappings are total functions\n862|  over uncoded inputs with no refused class to admit a member of;\n863|  tests pin them including real-exec scrub, stderr-capture, and\n864|  signal-death integrations. The signal-death arm (a killed child\n865|  errors instead of reporting -1 data) is a refused class and\n866|  carries its own narrowing row; the remaining mappings stay total.\n867|  Owner: this leaf.\n868|- B31 The custody root-ownership arm is untested and singleton: the\n869|  ownership seam stages leaf-first (the leaf refuses before the\n870|  root arm runs), and a truly foreign root needs privilege. Owner:\n871|  hardening with a privileged stage or a root-level seam.\n872|- B32 The leaf-delegation wiring is measured at CUS (wrong-leaf\n873|  mutants are observable only on compliant roots); the absence\n874|  propagation through the six dispatch paths, the prober, and the\n875|  spawner is pinned by absence tests without a row. Owner: this\n876|  leaf.\n877|- B33 The wrapper safe-boundary signal step is unimplemented in the\n878|  landed wrapper: the boundary entry waits blocking on\n879|  `ax-boundary-<generation>` for the wrapper's `wait-for -S`, and\n880|  the wrapper never signals today, so boundary waits time out with\n881|  the coded quiesce_timeout (fail closed, never a faked proof)\n882|  until the signal step lands. The wait vector, the proof-kind\n883|  binding, the provider-row context, and the timeout are this\n884|  leaf's and fully driven; the signal emission is the wrapper's.\n885|  Owner: the wrapper (`ax pane`) task; retest the full\n886|  quiesce-boundary-stop flow when the signal lands.\n887|- B34 A crash between the mutation-receipt commit and the operation\n888|  outcome record re-observes the report time on retry: the effect\n889|  never re-runs and the evidence never changes, but the reported\n890|  closure/boundary time renders from the retry clock instead of\n891|  the original one. Sequential retries without a crash replay\n892|  identical times. Before the retry heals the report, input can\n893|  reopen: attach consults the outcome proof, so the missing report\n894|  reads as no closure (bound B43 states the owner and the scoped\n895|  contract for the structural fix). Owner: this leaf for the\n896|  timestamp behavior; the receipt owner for the authority window.\n897|- B35 The absence stderr markers are verified against tmux 3.6a\n898|  (`can't find session`, `can't find window`, and the\n899|  no-such-socket connect error); any other version's\n900|  absence-shaped stderr fails closed to unknown. Owner: this leaf;\n901|  re-verify the marker set when the tmux floor version moves.\n902|- B36 The Execute dispatch and the ExecuteWrapperRestore entry pin\n903|  their dependency singletons without per-arm narrowing rows: a\n904|  nil lifecycle or a nil Runner, Receipts, Bindings, Attach,\n905|  States, CurrentLease, CurrentGeneration, or Now refuses\n906|  protocol-error before any decision or effect. Admitting one nil\n907|  arm is deleting the check. Owner: this leaf; retest if any site\n908|  grows a second refused member.\n909|- B37 No production mesh lease-refresh transport exists:\n910|  LeaseRefresh is an injected adapter (function field), and the\n911|  after-restore composition enforces the configured bound on any\n912|  adapter — cooperative or not — and rejects late answers even\n913|  with a nil error. The mesh RPC transport that would back a\n914|  production adapter is sibling scope (the mesh story); until it\n915|  lands, callers that need verified refreshes inject their own.\n916|  Owner: the mesh-refresh composition; retest the bound when a\n917|  production adapter lands.\n918|- B38 Union-rival ambiguity is unmodeled at the after-restore\n919|  composition: the entry decides over the single refreshed or\n920|  local winner, and a refresh adapter that observes rivals must\n921|  surface them as refresh failure so the entry parks unverified.\n922|  Owner: the mesh-refresh composition; retest when rivals are\n923|  modeled.\n924|- B39 Reachable-undriven: the entry reaches the gate but the\n925|  committed tests carry post-gate values only, so the refused\n926|  direction is undriven at that entry; the narrowed direction is\n927|  measured at the listed entry (\"M at ...\"). Formerly claimed\n928|  unreachable as U2b; stated as a bound now. Owner: this leaf;\n929|  drive a direction to move its cell to M.\n930|- B40 Lost incarnation rotation with a prior closure stays\n931|  closed with no production-entry recovery: the failed rotation\n932|  fails the operation closed, identical retries replay success\n933|  without rotating (rotating on replay would erase a genuine\n934|  newer closure), and a fresh key is unreachable because the\n935|  landed bootstrap store binds one bootstrap per session and the\n936|  receipt store refuses a second operation under a replayed key.\n937|  The stuck closure is over-strict in the safe direction; the\n938|  committed tests pin the failure, the replay skip, and the\n939|  bootstrap-store mechanism. A lost rotation with no prior\n940|  closure is harmless (the zero incarnation stays\n941|  self-consistent). Owner: axpane receipt/bootstrap contracts\n942|  for a repair entry; operator surgery clears the superseded\n943|  reports until one lands.\n944|- B41 The restore replay rotation skip is structural: the replay\n945|  branch contains no rotation code, so no narrowing mutant can\n946|  weaken it — the supplementary additive row\n947|  D-restore-replay-rotation inserts the forbidden write to prove\n948|  the committed replay test observes it. The create-side skip\n949|  has a narrowing row (N-create-replay-skip) because its\n950|  freshness condition is explicit code. Owner: this leaf; the\n951|  asymmetry is stated, not hidden.\n952|- B42 The input-closure ordering contract is in-process: the\n953|  barrier mutex serializes quiesce/boundary report commits\n954|  against attach receipt commits within one Lifecycle, but\n955|  concurrent ax processes racing attach against quiesce observe\n956|  only the report files, so a receipt committed in another\n957|  process's report-write window is not excluded. No committed\n958|  test stages two processes. Owner: this leaf; closing the\n959|  window needs cross-process exclusion (for example a lock file\n960|  under the state root). The vector handoff the contract covers\n961|  ends at vector construction: a caller that execs a\n962|  pre-quiescence vector after quiescence commits holds a\n963|  pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\n964|  The same in-process scope covers the attach post-lock\n965|  generation and deadline rechecks: a rotation landing between\n966|  the recheck and the commit — inside one process or across\n967|  processes — is not excluded; the window holds no waits.\n968|- B43 Closure authority has no single durable source. The engine\n969|  commits input closure and its receipt before this leaf records\n970|  the outcome report, and attach admission consults the outcome\n971|  proof alone, so a lost outcome-report write after committed\n972|  closure admits a fresh writable attach until the identical\n973|  retry heals the report: the failure to create the proof reads\n974|  as permission, and pending-versus-committed closure is not\n975|  representable in the outcome store. The same window covers a\n976|  crash between the receipt commit and the report, and a\n977|  simultaneous loss of both the report and the state record.\n978|  Retrying the identical quiesce heals the report and re-closes\n979|  input; no other production entry heals it. Closing the window\n980|  structurally needs the landed receipt owner\n981|  (internal/terminstance ReceiptStore) to expose\n982|  completed-closure enumeration — the completed quiesce/boundary\n983|  receipts for one instance, distinguishing\n984|  pending-without-completion from completed — so that attach\n985|  admission can consult receipt completion as the authoritative\n986|  proof. Owner: internal/terminstance for the enumeration\n987|  contract; this leaf for the admission side once it lands.\n988|  Until then the construction (incarnation-scoped proof,\n989|  advisory-memory split, in-process ordering) stands, and row 79\n990|  claims only the lost state-record write fails closed.\n991|- B44 Attach overlap is inferred from stored receipts, not\n992|  liveness: a recorded peer reads as possibly live, so the overlap\n993|  gate requires multi_attach (and multiple_input_clients for\n994|  concurrent input) even when the peer already detached, with\n995|  same-client retries exempt and unreadable peers failing closed.\n996|  The active-client census that refines the possibility —\n997|  overlap admission over live clients, with same-client retry\n998|  distinguished from a new client — is owned by\n999|  TASK-260922-vcx6yo (active-client-census-and-overlap-admission).\n1000|  Until it lands this leaf fails closed (over-strict) rather than\n1001|  admitting overlap without the capabilities. Owner:\n1002|  TASK-260922-vcx6yo for the census; this leaf for the fail-closed\n1003|  gate.\n1004|\n1005|Carried bounds (first-leaf statements dispositioned by this leaf).\n1006|B9 adapter split is discharged: the production exec, dial, probe,\n1007|and spawn adapters ship (exec.go, probe.go, backend.go) and\n1008|Production wires them into Dependencies; the residual is the\n1009|uncomposed wiring (B27). B16 nested invocation is decided: lifecycle\n1010|entries take no Ambient input, so nesting cannot collide through\n1011|them (row 90); the Acquire-level over-strict nested refusal stands\n1012|unchanged as first-leaf-owned. B18 sun_path is decided: strict-below\n1013|per platform, counted in bytes (row 66). B19/B20 bind step is built:\n1014|CheckSocketCustody enforces placement, leaf delegation, root,\n1015|ancestors, and socket kind (rows 67-70); the bind step refuses\n1016|intermediate symlinks through no-follow opens, which is stricter\n1017|than the B11 Acquire rule it stands beside. The rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy\n1018|foreground attach wiring is closed: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning\n1019|refuses every catalog-derived decoy alone and together on the\n1020|foreground running path with a spawn spy silent on every member, and\n1021|the attach attestation cells carry N-attach-attestation-decoy. New\n1022|bounds this revision: B33 states the unimplemented wrapper boundary\n1023|signal (fail-closed timeout until it lands), B34 the receipt/outcome\n1024|crash window, B35 the tmux-version marker set, B36 the dependency\n1025|singletons, B38 the unmodeled union rivals, and B39 the\n1026|reachable-undriven reclass. Revision 4 fills B37 (no production\n1027|mesh refresh transport; the composition enforces the bound on any\n1028|injected adapter), extends Table E with the binding, expiry, race,\n1029|and enforcement outcomes, and moves the SPW rootwrite cell from\n1030|B39 to measured. Revision 5 makes the incarnation-scoped closure\n1031|proof the sole barrier verdict (new Table D rows\n1032|barrierincarnation, barrierkey, attachhealth, failurerecord,\n1033|createincarnation, restoreincarnation, incarnationrecord,\n1034|incarnationlookup), extends Table E with the five composed-binding\n1035|refusals, moves the PRB rootwrite cell from B39 to measured, and\n1036|states B40 (stuck rotation) and B41 (structural replay skip).\n1037|Revision 6 adds the post-admission barrier recheck with the\n1038|in-process ordering lock (new Table D rows recheck and ordering;\n1039|attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1), the barrier read-error arms\n1040|(new Table D row barrierread; directory-read 1 / file-read 1),\n1041|moves the incarnationlookup EXA cell from B39 to measured, extends\n1042|the rootwrite EXA cell with the attach entry row, recounts Table C\n1043|from the Table D gate set (140 gates, 1540 cells), narrows row 79\n1044|to the lost state-record write with the outcome-report window\n1045|stated as B43 (receipt-owner enumeration contract), and states B42\n1046|(in-process ordering). Revision 7 closes the attach\n1047|admission-to-effect interval for every remaining live fact (the\n1048|post-lock generation and deadline rechecks with the full fact\n1049|enumeration; the authorization facts revalidate inside the\n1050|commit), moves the generation EXA cell from U1 to measured,\n1051|extends the deadline and authkind cells with the new rows,\n1052|reclassifies the two effect-loop authkind wirings as\n1053|supplementary D rows beside the genuine shared loop narrowing\n1054|N-lifecycle-loop-authorization, converts the entry authkind rows\n1055|to genuine no-bind narrowings, and extends B42 to the new\n1056|rechecks. Revision 8 closes the stop admission-to-effect interval\n1057|at the escalation boundary and the quiesce interval between its\n1058|commands (new Table D row effectrecheck; stop 4 / quiesce 4),\n1059|bounds every barrier and admission wait by the operation deadline\n1060|and cancellation (new Table D row waitbound; EXA 1 / EXE 1\n1061|shared), enforces the attach overlap capabilities fail-closed\n1062|over the stored peer census (new Table D rows overlapmulti and\n1063|overlapinput; liveness owned by TASK-260922-vcx6yo as B44),\n1064|reclassifies the entry-deadline instant row as\n1065|shadowed-supplementary (the wait bound refuses the same member),\n1066|extends B22 with the nil-recheck singleton, and recounts Table C\n1067|from the Table D gate set (144 gates, 1584 cells).","final_result":true}}}
