tted in another\n957|  process's report-write window is not excluded. No committed\n958|  test stages two processes. Owner: this leaf; closing the\n959|  window needs cross-process exclusion (for example a lock file\n960|  under the state root). The vector handoff the contract covers\n961|  ends at vector construction: a caller that execs a\n962|  pre-quiescence vector after quiescence commits holds a\n963|  pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\n964|  The same in-process scope covers the attach post-lock\n965|  generation and deadline rechecks: a rotation landing between\n966|  the recheck and the commit — inside one process or across\n967|  processes — is not excluded; the window holds no waits.\n968|- B43 Closure authority has no single durable source. The engine\n969|  commits input closure and its receipt before this leaf records\n970|  the outcome report, and attach admission consults the outcome\n971|  proof alone, so a lost outcome-report write after committed\n972|  closure admits a fresh writable attach until the identical\n973|  retry heals the report: the failure to create the proof reads\n974|  as permission, and pending-versus-committed closure is not\n975|  representable in the outcome store. The same window covers a\n976|  crash between the receipt commit and the report, and a\n977|  simultaneous loss of both the report and the state record.\n978|  Retrying the identical quiesce heals the report and re-closes\n979|  input; no other production entry heals it. Closing the window\n980|  structurally needs the landed receipt owner\n981|  (internal/terminstance ReceiptStore) to expose\n982|  completed-closure enumeration — the completed quiesce/boundary\n983|  receipts for one instance, distinguishing\n984|  pending-without-completion from completed — so that attach\n985|  admission can consult receipt completion as the authoritative\n986|  proof. Owner: internal/terminstance for the enumeration\n987|  contract; this leaf for the admission side once it lands.\n988|  Until then the construction (incarnation-scoped proof,\n989|  advisory-memory split, in-process ordering) stands, and row 79\n990|  claims only the lost state-record write fails closed.\n991|- B44 Attach overlap is inferred from stored receipts, not\n992|  liveness: a recorded peer reads as possibly live, so the overlap\n993|  gate requires multi_attach (and multiple_input_clients for\n994|  concurrent input) even when the peer already detached, with\n995|  same-client retries exempt and unreadable peers failing closed.\n996|  The active-client census that refines the possibility —\n997|  overlap admission over live clients, with same-client retry\n998|  distinguished from a new client — is owned by\n999|  TASK-260922-vcx6yo (active-client-census-and-overlap-admission).\n1000|  Until it lands this leaf fails closed (over-strict) rather than\n1001|  admitting overlap without the capabilities. Owner:\n1002|  TASK-260922-vcx6yo for the census; this leaf for the fail-closed\n1003|  gate.\n1004|\n1005|Carried bounds (first-leaf statements dispositioned by this leaf).\n1006|B9 adapter split is discharged: the production exec, dial, probe,\n1007|and spawn adapters ship (exec.go, probe.go, backend.go) and\n1008|Production wires them into Dependencies; the residual is the\n1009|uncomposed wiring (B27). B16 nested invocation is decided: lifecycle\n1010|entries take no Ambient input, so nesting cannot collide through\n1011|them (row 90); the Acquire-level over-strict nested refusal stands\n1012|unchanged as first-leaf-owned. B18 sun_path is decided: strict-below\n1013|per platform, counted in bytes (row 66). B19/B20 bind step is built:\n1014|CheckSocketCustody enforces placement, leaf delegation, root,\n1015|ancestors, and socket kind (rows 67-70); the bind step refuses\n1016|intermediate symlinks through no-follow opens, which is stricter\n1017|than the B11 Acquire rule it stands beside. The rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy\n1018|foreground attach wiring is closed: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning\n1019|refuses every catalog-derived decoy alone and together on the\n1020|foreground running path with a spawn spy silent on every member, and\n1021|the attach attestation cells carry N-attach-attestation-decoy. New\n1022|bounds this revision: B33 states the unimplemented wrapper boundary\n1023|signal (fail-closed timeout until it lands), B34 the receipt/outcome\n1024|crash window, B35 the tmux-version marker set, B36 the dependency\n1025|singletons, B38 the unmodeled union rivals, and B39 the\n1026|reachable-undriven reclass. Revision 4 fills B37 (no production\n1027|mesh refresh transport; the composition enforces the bound on any\n1028|injected adapter), extends Table E with the binding, expiry, race,\n1029|and enforcement outcomes, and moves the SPW rootwrite cell from\n1030|B39 to measured. Revision 5 makes the incarnation-scoped closure\n1031|proof the sole barrier verdict (new Table D rows\n1032|barrierincarnation, barrierkey, attachhealth, failurerecord,\n1033|createincarnation, restoreincarnation, incarnationrecord,\n1034|incarnationlookup), extends Table E with the five composed-binding\n1035|refusals, moves the PRB rootwrite cell from B39 to measured, and\n1036|states B40 (stuck rotation) and B41 (structural replay skip).\n1037|Revision 6 adds the post-admission barrier recheck with the\n1038|in-process ordering lock (new Table D rows recheck and ordering;\n1039|attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1), the barrier read-error arms\n1040|(new Table D row barrierread; directory-read 1 / file-read 1),\n1041|moves the incarnationlookup EXA cell from B39 to measured, extends\n1042|the rootwrite EXA cell with the attach entry row, recounts Table C\n1043|from the Table D gate set (140 gates, 1540 cells), narrows row 79\n1044|to the lost state-record write with the outcome-report window\n1045|stated as B43 (receipt-owner enumeration contract), and states B42\n1046|(in-process ordering). Revision 7 closes the attach\n1047|admission-to-effect interval for every remaining live fact (the\n1048|post-lock generation and deadline rechecks with the full fact\n1049|enumeration; the authorization facts revalidate inside the\n1050|commit), moves the generation EXA cell from U1 to measured,\n1051|extends the deadline and authkind cells with the new rows,\n1052|reclassifies the two effect-loop authkind wirings as\n1053|supplementary D rows beside the genuine shared loop narrowing\n1054|N-lifecycle-loop-authorization, converts the entry authkind rows\n1055|to genuine no-bind narrowings, and extends B42 to the new\n1056|rechecks. Revision 8 closes the stop admission-to-effect interval\n1057|at the escalation boundary and the quiesce interval between its\n1058|commands (new Table D row effectrecheck; stop 4 / quiesce 4),\n1059|bounds every barrier and admission wait by the operation deadline\n1060|and cancellation (new Table D row waitbound; EXA 1 / EXE 1\n1061|shared), enforces the attach overlap capabilities fail-closed\n1062|over the stored peer census (new Table D rows overlapmulti and\n1063|overlapinput; liveness owned by TASK-260922-vcx6yo as B44),\n1064|reclassifies the entry-deadline instant row as\n1065|shadowed-supplementary (the wait bound refuses the same member),\n1066|extends B22 with the nil-recheck singleton, and recounts Table C\n1067|from the Table D gate set (144 gates, 1584 cells).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
