{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb7d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":1049,"recorded_at":1780531400002093,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9ae-ef53-7762-ba70-517971ded38c"},"task_id":"01a0c9ae-ef53-7762-ba70-517971ded38c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9ae-ef53-7762-ba70-517971ded38c","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/tmuxserver.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer tests must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence; the six D- rows are\n8|explicitly supplementary and not counted as any gate's narrowing: three\n9|additive plants (D-background-fallback,\n10|D-background-fallback-foreground, D-restore-replay-rotation), two\n11|positive-path wiring checks (D-lifecycle-restore-authkind,\n12|D-lifecycle-terminate-authkind), and one shadowed narrowing\n13|(D-attach-entry-deadline-shadowed, which survives by reroute to the\n14|wait bound), each labeled as such in its note.\n15|\n16|Each row runs M (mutate production files in place), R (run the scoped Go\n17|killers through the production entries), V (verdict from the Go exit code\n18|plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test failure line,\n19|SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else -- unapplied patches,\n20|build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R infrastructure errors are\n21|ERROR, never kills or survivals. Files are restored from backups after\n22|every row, pass or fail.\n23|\n24|Row C-control is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that must\n25|SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n26|hard-coding kills.\n27|\n28|Usage:\n29|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\n30|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py N-mode-create\n31|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py --log-dir /tmp/mutant-logs\n32|  AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py N-mode-create\n33|\"\"\"\n34|\n35|import os\n36|import shutil\n37|import subprocess\n38|import sys\n39|import tempfile\n40|from dataclasses import dataclass\n41|from pathlib import Path\n42|\n43|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n44|PACKAGE = \"internal/tmuxserver\"\n45|\n46|\n47|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n48|class Mutant:\n49|    name: str\n50|    path: str\n51|    find: str\n52|    replace: str\n53|    count: int\n54|    run: str\n55|    expect: str\n56|    note: str\n57|\n58|\n59|BG_MISS = \"TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable\"\n60|BG_MISS_LINUX = \"(TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable|TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback)\"\n61|OVERRIDE = \"TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector\"\n62|RES_OVERRIDE = \"(TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector|TestResolveSocketRefusesEveryOverrideVector)\"\n63|WIDENED = \"TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode\"\n64|COLLISION = \"(TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision|TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision)\"\n65|\n66|MUTANTS = [\n67|    Mutant(\n68|        name=\"N-mode-create\",\n69|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/runtime_unix.go\",\n70|        find=\"\\t// leaf above; the mode comparison below is the load-bearing\\n\\t// arm this gate's tests and mutants pin.\\n\\tif info.Mode().Perm() != 0o700 {\\n\",\n71|        replace=\"\\t// leaf above; the mode comparison below is the load-bearing\\n\\t// arm this gate's tests and mutants pin.\\n\\tif info.Mode().Perm() != 0o700 && info.Mode().Perm() != 0o755 {\\n\",\n72|        count=1,\n73|        run=WIDENED,\n74|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n75|        note=\"Admits exactly 0755 at the create-path mode arm; other widened modes still refuse. Kill path: Ensure stops refusing.\",\n76|    ),\n77|    Mutant(\n78|        name=\"N-mode-verify\",\n79|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/runtime_unix.go\",\n80|        find='\\tinfo, err := leaf.Stat()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn &Error{Code: CodeUnsafeRuntimeDir, Detail: \"runtime mode\"}\\n\\t}\\n\\tif info.Mode().Perm() != 0o700 {\\n',\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
