{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb81","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":1051,"recorded_at":1780531400002097,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9ae-ef30-7b22-803e-2a355e4265a0"},"task_id":"01a0c9ae-ef30-7b22-803e-2a355e4265a0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9ae-ef30-7b22-803e-2a355e4265a0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TRACEABILITY — internal/termbind (AX v0.7.0)\n2|\n3|Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.B (Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0\n4|closed object and the identity rule), Section 5.2 Session Event 4.0.0\n5|Terminal Instance events (terminal.created and session.resumed v4\n6|payloads), Section 4.D (evidence binding), Section 7.A (Provider\n7|Protocol 3 descriptor identity, cited landed), and Section 13.1\n8|(bootstrap idempotency and lost-result recovery). Story:\n9|ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding (final leaf).\n10|\n11|Rule: every row names its production entry point. A row is driven only\n12|when the named committed test executes that entry. Prose in place of\n13|the ratio is not evidence. 66 of 67 AC rows driven; row 57 is a stated\n14|bound (payload census — no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk to drive).\n15|\n16|## Identity and the Binding object (Section 4.B, Section 7.A)\n17|\n18|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n19||---|--------|-----------|------|\n20|| 1 | UUIDv7 admitted as terminal instance identity | CheckInstanceIdentity (identity.go) | TestCheckInstanceIdentityAdmitsUUIDv7 |\n21|| 2 | Eight forbidden forms (PID, handle, socket, path, pipe, URL, token, endpoint) refuse terminal_backend_protocol_error | CheckInstanceIdentity (identity.go) | TestCheckInstanceIdentityRefusesForbiddenForms (8 subtests) |\n22|| 3 | Closed Binding fixture admitted with literal members | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingAdmitsClosedFixture |\n23|| 4 | Eight forbidden forms in terminal_instance_id refuse the pinned code | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingRefusesForbiddenIdentity (8 subtests) |\n24|| 5 | Binding closed shape (missing/extra/duplicate member, wrong schema) refuses | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape (4 subtests) |\n25|| 61 | Every Binding member arm refuses with its code and detail (schema/schema_version/binding_id/session/host/incarnation/instance/backend-ID/impl/protocol/generation/native/created/supersedes/extensions value arms, non-object frame, trailing data) | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingMemberArms (37 subtests) |\n26|| 62 | Hostile extension literals (JSON numbers, nested duplicate) refuse at the extensions arm; lone surrogate refuses at the frame | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingRawExtensions (6 subtests) |\n27|| 63 | Identity pre-transform walk refuses numbers, nested duplicates, trailing data, non-object, depth and size caps; clean digest equals | bindingIdentity (identity.go) | TestBindingIdentityRefusesHostileBytes (12 subtests + clean) |\n28|| 64 | Identity verdicts and the protocol-major verdict agree with the landed rules | bindingIdentity (identity.go), isProtocolMajorOne (identity.go) | TestBindingIdentityVerdictAgreesWithLandedAdmission (2 subtests), TestBindingProtocolMajorAgreesWithLandedTuple (14 subtests) |\n29|| 6 | Binding backend_generation 256 admits, 0 and 257 refuse | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/generation_bounds |\n30|| 7 | Binding native_reference 512 admits, 0 and 513 refuse | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/native_reference_bounds |\n31|| 8 | Tampered member and wrong self ID refuse terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch | ParseTerminalBinding (identity.go) | TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape (tampered, wrong_self_id) |\n32|| 9 | Binding identity construction agrees with the landed manifest admission | bindingIdentity via ParseManifest (identity.go) | TestBindingIdentityAgreesWithLandedAdmission |\n33|| 10 | Eight forbidden forms in the Provider Protocol 3 descriptor refuse the pinned code | AdmitProviderDescriptor, adopted landed (terminalbackend/descriptor.go) | TestAdmitDescriptorRefusesForbiddenIdentity (8 subtests) |\n34|| 11 | Eight forbidden forms in the mutation context refuse the pinned code (documented redundancy: the landed parser refuses the same code; the wrapper adds the Go error type) | AdmitMutationContext (identity.go) | TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity (8 subtests) |\n35|| 12 | Eight forbidden forms in the status body refuse the pinned code (same redundancy); null instance admitted | AdmitStatusBody (identity.go) | TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity (8 subtests + null) |\n36|| 13 | Non-string identity members delegate to the landed shape authority | AdmitMutationContext, AdmitStatusBody (identity.go) | TestAdmitSurfacesDelegateShapeFaults (2 subtests) |\n37|| 14 | Eight forbidden forms in the bootstrap binding refuse and persist nothing | Store.Bind, adopted (axpane/binding.go) | TestBootstrapBindingRefusesForbiddenIdentity (8 subtests) |\n38|| 15 | CLI Result 4.0.0 identity surface is a stated bound pinned by a tripwire | VersionForCommand, cited (cliresult) | TestCLIResult4IdentityIsUnimplementedBound |\n39|\n40|## Binding succession (Section 4.B identity, Section 4.C restore)\n41|\n42|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n43||---|--------|-----------|------|\n44|| 67 | MintSuccessorBinding mints the reboot-successor binding over a parsed prior: malformed and same-generation mints refuse, the successor names the new generation, links the prior binding id via supersedes_binding_id, recomputes the omit-self identity, re-admits its own image before return, and mints deterministically so a crash between the restore effects and the successor persist converges on retry | MintSuccessorBinding (successor.go) | TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations, TestMintSuccessorBindingIsDeterministic, TestMintSuccessorBindingRefusesSameGeneration, TestMintSuccessorBindingRefusesMalformedGeneration, TestMintSuccessorBindingIdentityBinds |\n45|| 68 | Peers replays the stored peer census for one terminal instance except the requesting client: every recorded receipt except the caller's own, sorted by client ID, with no liveness decided. An unrecorded instance has no peers; staging files are skipped; a read, decode, or binding failure errors instead of reading as an empty census. | Peers (overlap.go) | TestAttachStorePeers, TestAttachStorePeersEmpty, TestAttachStorePeersFailsClosed, TestAttachStorePeersRejectsForeignReceipt |\n46|\n47|## Evidence resolution (Section 4.D, Section 5.2)\n48|\n49|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n50||---|--------|-----------|------|\n51|| 16 | Coherent universe resolves to manifest, probe, evidence, and admission | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceAdmitsUniverse |\n52|| 17 | Empty and 257-element evidence sets refuse the 1..256 bound | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds (empty, 257) |\n53|| 18 | Unsorted, duplicate, and non-digest evidence sets refuse | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds (unsorted, duplicate, non-digest) |\n54|| 19 | One digest passes the shape and refuses at the manifest/probe partition | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/one_passes_shape_to_partition |\n55|| 20 | 256 digests pass the shape and refuse at lookup | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/256_passes_shape_to_lookup |\n56|| 21 | Eleven foreign resolution targets refuse the mismatch class | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceRefusesForeignKinds (11 subtests) |\n57|| 22 | Missing or doubled manifest/probe refuses the stated cardinality | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe (4 subtests) |\n58|| 23 | Foreign-backend and protocol-drift evidence refuse at this gate | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceBindsEventTuple (2 subtests) |\n59|| 24 | Document substitution under another ID refuses | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceRejectsSubstitution (2 subtests) |\n60|| 25 | Admission faults (unevidenced claim, forged signature, expiry, registry drift) surface landed | ResolveEvidence via Registry.AdmitProbe (resolve.go) | TestResolveEvidenceDrivesLandedAdmission (4 subtests) |\n61|| 26 | Resolved objects carry no live-process fact | ResolveEvidence (resolve.go) | TestResolvedObjectsCarryNoLiveFacts |\n62|\n63|## Emission (Section 5.2)\n64|\n65|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n66||---|--------|-----------|------|\n67|| 27 | terminal.created v4 round-trips through the append path | EmitTerminalCreated (emit.go) | TestEmitTerminalCreatedRoundTrip |\n68|| 28 | session.resumed v4 round-trips (null and carried source); bad profile refuses | EmitResumed (emit.go) | TestEmitResumedRoundTrip (3 subtests) |\n69|| 66 | Caller-bound checkpoint/pair boundary pinned: a fabricated checkpoint appends and the fold reports it newest (the wrapper supplies both from the fold; CheckResumedPair uncomposed — stated bound) | EmitResumed (emit.go) | TestEmitResumedCheckpointBindingIsCallerBound |\n70|| 29 | Unsorted and empty evidence refuse at the emission entries | EmitTerminalCreated (emit.go) | TestEmitClosedShapeRefusals (unsorted, empty) |\n71|| 30 | Missing/extra payload members refuse at the canonical boundary | Emit, adopted (axpane/events.go) | TestEmitClosedShapeRefusals (3 append subtests) |\n72|| 31 | Unresolvable and foreign evidence refuse inside both emission entries | EmitTerminalCreated, EmitResumed (emit.go) | TestEmitResolvesEvidence (3 subtests) |\n73|| 32 | Losing lease refuses and appends nothing | EmitTerminalCreated via Emit (emit.go) | TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses |\n74|| 33 | Byte-identical retry replays the one event | EmitTerminalCreated (emit.go) | TestEmitAppendsIdempotently |\n75|| 34 | Emitted bytes carry the opaque digest and no binding secret | EmitTerminalCreated (emit.go) | TestEmittedEventCarriesNoBindingObject |\n76|\n77|## Recovery (Section 13.1)\n78|\n79|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n80||---|--------|-----------|------|\n81|| 35 | No binding plus proven absence yields absence with replay_same | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateProvesAbsence |\n82|| 36 | Binding plus matching live status yields the ONE child | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateIdentifiesOneChild (2 subtests) |\n83|| 37 | Duplicate retry yields the identical verdict | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateDuplicateRetrySameVerdict |\n84|| 38 | Changed operation in the fold-derived open window refuses idempotency_mismatch | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateChangedOperationInWindowRefuses |\n85|| 39 | Changed operation in the fold-derived closed window proceeds | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateChangedOperationPostWindowProceeds |\n86|| 40 | Lost create result recovers the ONE recorded child | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateLostResult |\n87|| 41 | Five unprovable shapes yield unavailable with status_first, never absence | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent (5 subtests) |\n88|| 42 | Recorded child with a backend-absent observation replays the same pair | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateRecordedChildBackendAbsentReplays |\n89|| 43 | Status read failure is an error, never absence | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateUnknownIsNotAbsent |\n90|| 65 | 257-character generation refuses the landed bound before the status read runs | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverGenerationBoundBeforeStatusRead |\n91|\n92|## Attach receipts (Section 4.C attach, Section 4.E)\n93|\n94|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n95||---|--------|-----------|------|\n96|| 44 | Attach records and replays one receipt per client pair | AttachStore.Attach/Lookup (attach.go) | TestAttachRoundTrip |\n97|| 45 | Identical retry replays the recorded receipt | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachIdenticalRetryReplays |\n98|| 46 | Second client records alongside, never over | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachSecondClientRecordsAlongside |\n99|| 47 | Transport/input conflict refuses idempotency_mismatch | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachConflictRefusesMismatch |\n100|| 48 | Sixteen forbidden identity values refuse the pinned code | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachRefusesForbiddenIdentity (16 subtests) |\n101|| 49 | Unknown transport refuses; relay refuses by landed policy | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachTransportVocabulary (2 subtests) |\n102|| 50 | Expired, mismatched, and malformed policy refuses on every call | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachRequiresLiveAuth (4 subtests) |\n103|| 51 | Attach emits neither event nor lease/fencing change | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachEmitsNeitherEventNorStateChange |\n104|| 52 | Torn receipt is an error, never absence | AttachStore.Attach/Lookup (attach.go) | TestAttachUnknownIsNotAbsent |\n105|| 53 | Foreign-session lookup refuses | AttachStore.Lookup (attach.go) | TestAttachSessionMismatchRefuses |\n106|\n107|## Version skew and authority (Section 5.2)\n108|\n109|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n110||---|--------|-----------|------|\n111|| 54 | Takeover selects an admitted backend with a new digest and event, append-only, no fork | EmitTerminalCreated, EmitResumed (emit.go) | TestTakeoverSelectsNewBackendNewEvent |\n112|| 55 | v1 and v4 terminal events derive exactly their own surface | Reduce, adopted (sessstate) | TestVersionSelectionBothDirections (3 subtests) |\n113|| 56 | v4 retained verbatim, no lower-version replacement, query reads derive nothing new | GetEvent/ListEvents, Reader.List, adopted (sessrepo, sessquery) | TestV4RetainedAsImmutableHistory |\n114|| 57 | STATED BOUND: v4 carries no v1 derivation member (payload census); a v1-only reader staying inert cannot be driven — no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk (the retained-verbatim half is row 56) | DecodeEvent, adopted (sessstate) | TestV1ReaderSeesV4AsInert (census, not a reader drive) |\n115|\n116|## Crash and idempotency seams\n117|\n118|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n119||---|--------|-----------|------|\n120|| 58 | SIGKILL after the receipt commit leaves the complete receipt; retry replays | AttachStore.Attach (attach.go) | TestAttachCrashChildSelfTerminates (unix) |\n121|| 59 | SIGKILL between effect and result recovers the ONE child | RecoverCreate (recover.go) | TestRecoverCreateAfterKillRecoversChild (unix) |\n122|| 60 | Before-write abort leaves no event; after-commit keeps and replays | EmitTerminalCreated (emit.go) | TestEmitAppendHookSeams (2 subtests) |\n123|\n124|## Mutant table (40 rows: 38 narrowing + 1 supplementary arm-delete + 1 control)\n125|\n126|Harness: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3\n127|internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py`. Verdict rule (M/R/V): R fails\n128|with a test failure line means KILLED; R passes means SURVIVED; an\n129|unapplied patch, build break, or timeout is ERROR. All rows pass 1,\n130|mutants/pass2.\n131|\n132|| ID | Kind | Plant | Killer |\n133||----|------|-------|--------|\n134|| N-identity-pid | narrowing | CheckInstanceIdentity admits \"12345\" | TestCheckInstanceIdentityRefusesForbiddenForms, TestParseTerminalBindingRefusesForbiddenIdentity, TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity, TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity, TestAttachRefusesForbiddenIdentity |\n135|| N-identity-endpoint | narrowing | CheckInstanceIdentity admits \"10.0.0.9:2222\" | same five surfaces |\n136|| N-binding-members | narrowing | ParseTerminalBinding admits one extra member | TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/extra_member |\n137|| N-binding-identity | narrowing | ParseTerminalBinding admits the wrong self-ID fixture | TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/wrong_self_id |\n138|| N-binding-generation | narrowing | ParseTerminalBinding admits the 257-character generation | TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/generation_bounds |\n139|| N-binding-protocol-major | narrowing | ParseTerminalBinding admits protocol 2.0.0 past the major-1 arm | TestParseTerminalBindingMemberArms/protocol_version_major_2 |\n140|| N-binding-extensions | narrowing | ParseTerminalBinding admits the one-key note extensions object | TestParseTerminalBindingMemberArms/extensions_non-empty |\n141|| N-binding-identity-number | narrowing | Identity walk admits the 1.0 number | TestBindingIdentityRefusesHostileBytes/float |\n142|| N-binding-nested-dup | narrowing | Identity decode admits nested duplicates | TestBindingIdentityRefusesHostileBytes/nested_duplicate |\n143|| N-binding-supersedes | narrowing | ParseTerminalBinding admits the not-a-digest supersedes value | TestParseTerminalBindingMemberArms/supersedes_non-digest |\n144|| N-prescan-context | narrowing | AdmitMutationContext skips the gate for \"12345\" | TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity/pid |\n145|| N-status-prescan | narrowing | AdmitStatusBody skips the gate for \"12345\" | TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity/pid |\n146|| N-evidence-257 | narrowing | Shape admits 257 IDs | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/257_refuses |\n147|| N-evidence-0 | narrowing | Shape admits the empty set | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/empty_refuses |\n148|| N-evidence-dup | narrowing | Order admits duplicates | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/duplicate_refuses |\n149|| N-evidence-unsorted | narrowing | Order skips the first-pair comparison | TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/unsorted_refuses |\n150|| N-resolve-kind | narrowing | Resolution admits the endpoint document | TestResolveEvidenceRefusesForeignKinds/endpoint, TestEmitResolvesEvidence/foreign_kind |\n151|| N-resolve-manifest-count | narrowing | Partition admits the four-ID double manifest | TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe/second_manifest |\n152|| N-resolve-binding | narrowing | Binding drops the evidence protocol arm | TestResolveEvidenceBindsEventTuple/protocol_drift_evidence |\n153|| N-resolve-identity | narrowing | Substitution check drops the probe half | TestResolveEvidenceRejectsSubstitution/probe_alias |\n154|| N-resolve-admission | narrowing | Resolution swallows the landed drift refusal | TestResolveEvidenceDrivesLandedAdmission/registry_drift |\n155|| N-emit-created-v3 | narrowing | Created event emitted at v3 | TestEmitTerminalCreatedRoundTrip |\n156|| N-emit-resumed-v3 | narrowing | Resumed event emitted at v3 | TestEmitResumedRoundTrip |\n157|| D-emit-noresolve | arm-delete, supplementary | Resolution dropped at both emission entries | TestEmitResolvesEvidence |\n158|| N-recover-mismatch | narrowing | Recovery admits the fixture changed operation | TestRecoverCreateChangedOperationInWindowRefuses |\n159|| N-recover-second-child | narrowing | Unbound live instance adopted as a child | TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent/unbound_live_instance |\n160|| N-recover-contradiction-absent | narrowing | Bound contradiction claimed as absence | TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent/bound_contradiction |\n161|| N-recover-creating-child | narrowing | Creating interim admitted as a child | TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent/creating_interim |\n162|| N-recover-status-error | narrowing | Status read failure laundered as absence | TestRecoverCreateUnknownIsNotAbsent/status_read_failure |\n163|| N-recover-window | narrowing | Window bit inverted | TestRecoverCreateChangedOperationInWindowRefuses |\n164|| N-recover-generation | narrowing | Generation bound skipped for the 257-character generation before the status read | TestRecoverGenerationBoundBeforeStatusRead |\n165|| N-attach-conflict | narrowing | Conflict drops the input half at both comparisons | TestAttachConflictRefusesMismatch |\n166|| N-attach-transport | narrowing | Enum admits smoke_signal | TestAttachTransportVocabulary/unknown_transport |\n167|| N-attach-auth-replay | narrowing | Replay skips authorization | TestAttachRequiresLiveAuth/replay_with_expired_auth |\n168|| N-attach-key | narrowing | Idempotency key drops the client axis | TestAttachSecondClientRecordsAlongside |\n169|| N-successor-same-generation | narrowing | Successor mint admits the fixture same generation | TestMintSuccessorBindingRefusesSameGeneration, TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations |\n170|| N-successor-supersedes | narrowing | Successor omits its prior link | TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations |\n171|| N-successor-identity-field | narrowing | Successor identity omits the wrong field | TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations, TestMintSuccessorBindingIdentityBinds |\n172|| N-successor-generation-inherit | narrowing | Successor names the prior generation | TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations, TestMintSuccessorBindingRefusesSameGeneration |\n173|| N-attach-peers-decode | narrowing | Peer scan skips the undecodable receipt | TestAttachStorePeersFailsClosed |\n174|| C-control | control | Comment-only doc edit | TestCheckInstanceIdentityAdmitsUUIDv7 (SURVIVED) |\n175|\n176|Not rows, by construction: attach cannot emit an event because Attach\n177|takes no repository (proven by row 51 — no text plant can add a write);\n178|the lease-authority narrowing belongs to the adopted axpane rows\n179|N-emit-mutation and N-emit-losing-epoch (composition pinned by row 32);\n180|the descriptor identity gate is landed and narrowed by the\n181|terminalbackend owner (this leaf drives its eight forms through the\n182|landed entry in row 10).\n183|\n184|## Stated contracts and bounds\n185|\n186|- Resolution cardinality: exactly one Manifest and exactly one Probe per\n187|  event (the specification pins the resolution requirement but not the\n188|  cardinality; ambiguity fails closed). Rows 19, 22.\n189|- The bootstrap window bit is caller-derived from the sessstate fold's\n190|  newest checkpoint; recovery tests close the loop by folding a real\n191|  chain (rows 38, 39) instead of forking the loader.\n192|- CLI Result 4.0.0 is registered but unimplemented in internal/cliresult\n193|  (owner: cliresult); the Result 4 identity surface is NOT APPLICABLE\n194|  with a tripwire that fails if Result 4 ever lands (row 15).\n195|- Restore/terminate-stale engine execution remains refused by the\n196|  terminstance scope gates; recovery in this leaf covers the Section 4.1\n197|  bootstrap (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) create row. Executing\n198|  restore/terminate-stale is deferred to a Story follow-up task (no board\n199|  task exists yet — no brief in this Story assigned it).\n200|- The kkh1an `HandoffFailed` reporter note is NOT APPLICABLE: this leaf\n201|  wires no `HandoffFailed` reporter (only tests set the member).\n202|- EmitResumed binds neither checkpoint_id to the chain nor the\n203|  (profile, source) pair to the referenced checkpoint's closure via\n204|  sessprofile.CheckResumedPair; the wrapper decision supplies both from\n205|  the fold, and the direct-caller boundary is pinned (row 66).\n206|- The v1-only-reader half of 5.2#18 is a stated bound: no v1-v3-only\n207|  reader exists on trunk, so row 57 is a payload census and the\n208|  retained-verbatim half (row 56) carries the drive.\n209|- The operation-body pre-scans (rows 11, 12) are a documented\n210|  redundancy: the landed parsers refuse the same pinned code, and the\n211|  wrappers add only the Go error type their narrowing rows kill on.\n212|- No `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider\n213|  process, and no mesh transport live in this package.","final_result":true}}}
