battery (34 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\\n2365:## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\\n2367:[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\\n2439:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n2440:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n2443:Run the narrowing battery (286 narrowing mutants, six supplementary\\n2449:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n2457:attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`, with the lifecycle battery and its\\n2462:[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n2508:Run the falsification battery (8 narrowing mutants plus three controls) with:\\n===LOGBOOK-HEAD===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed\\n\\n- P1-A FIXED (stop escalation + quiesce mid-sequence): the stop escalation revalidates the operation deadline, AX authorization over the live lease, and server generation after its poll before `kill-session` issues — a graceful timeout escalates, any other stale fact refuses without the kill — and the quiesce detach revalidates between the lock and detach commands. The two post-wait boundaries share one closure over the landed gates (same `CheckAuthorization` call, same generation read, row's own timeout code) with per-site skip narrowings; sibling paths probed with fact-mutation during their waits: create/restore single-command (rotation changes nothing), terminate tail (kill count stays one, refusal stands), boundary tail (post-signal command is the read-only rows probe). Graceful wait and operation deadline are distinct bounds. Narrowings: 3 shared arms + 2 per-site skips, all KILLED with per-test attribution; census effectrecheck stop 4 / quiesce 4.\\n- P2 FIXED (bounded waits, uniform barrier contract): the attach admission and barrier acquisition run under one wait context combining the operation deadline with caller cancellation — the entry bounds the wait itself (goroutine + select, late answers discarded), so even a non-cooperative adapter cannot hold the request past its deadline or commit late. Quiesce span and boundary report commit acquire through the same contract (row's own timeout code; boundary reports against its committed proof). Release-controlled tests prove refusal-before-release plus no-late-receipt; cancellation returns promptly. Narrowing `N-attach-wait-deadline` KILLED through all four deadline tests while the cancellation companion stays green.\\n- P1-B NARROWED (overlap fail-closed): this leaf has no liveness census, so a stored peer receipt reads as possibly live — a second client needs `multi_attach`, new input over an input peer needs `multiple_input_clients`, same-client retries exempt, unreadable peers fail closed. Over-strict by design (detached clients' receipts still trigger) until the liveness census lands; owner TASK-260922-vcx6yo, stated as B44. Narrowings `N-attach-overlap-multi` / `-input` KILLED with two-peer precision legs. The §4.C attach row claims only the fail-closed gate, never liveness.\\n- PROCESS: a new downstream bound shadows an upstream narrowing when it refuses the same member with the same verdict — the entry-deadline instant row is reclassified as survived-supplementary `D-attach-entry-deadline-shadowed` (enforced boundary measured at post-lock + wait), with deterministic fired-context pre-checks so the shadowing never races. An ordering-lock plant must skip the acquisition, not acquire-then-release (the wait alone preserves the order and the row survives). Census: 261 measured of 5376 (new rows effectrecheck/overlapmulti/overlapinput/waitbound), battery 293/293 + 41/41.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev7 — attach effect-boundary enumeration; authkind evidence repair\\n\\n- P1+P2-A FIXED (same invariant, one enumeration): the attach admission-to-effect interval that rev6 closed for closure stayed open for generation and the request deadline. The post-lock boundary now revalidates every live fact — closure (existing recheck), server generation (new live `CurrentGeneration` read), request deadline (new live clock read, lock wait counted, kept distinct from authorization expiry) — while authorization expiry, transport, and input binding revalidate inside the commit call itself (`AttachStore.Attach` rechecks with the live clock and holds no wait before the no-replace install); transition, operation capability, and backend identity are pure checks over request-immutable members with nothing to revalidate. SPEC §4.C 1095 (\\\"rechecked immediately before each side effect\\\") is the pin. Regressions: rotation-during-lock-wait (channel-ordered, deterministic), admission-advances-clock-past-deadline with valid authorization, and the on-the-instant variant. Narrowings `N-attach-postlock-generation` / `N-attach-postlock-deadline` KILLED; sibling members (late instants) still refuse under the plants. Create/restore/stop never had the interval: the landed engine `runEffects` and this leaf's `runLifecycleEffects` recheck deadline+authorization+generation before every effect including the first, after any wait. Residual (B42 extended): a rotation between the recheck and the commit, in- or cross-process, in a wait-free window.\\n- P2-B CLOSED: `TestAttachAuthorizationMembersRefuseWithoutReceipt` (expiry/input/transport) asserts refusal AND receipt absence through `Execute(attach)`; `N-attach-input-escalation` (reviewer A3 shape on the landed gate, cross-package row) commits the receipt before the result binding refuses, so the killer's absence assertion reddens. Gate stays landed, no fork.\\n- P3 CLOSED: the two effect-loop authkind wirings are reclassified as supplementary `D-` rows (they refuse a permitted grant; they admit nothing), the entry authkind rows are converted to genuine no-bind narrowings (control-kind bodies bind under the plant and refuse only at the loop), and the shared loop side is measured by the genuinely admitting `N-lifecycle-loop-authorization` (pre-commit auth failures execute the first effect; post-commit still refuse), killing through both terminate and restore entries with per-entry attribution. Census: 256 measured of 5248 (generation EXA U1→M), symmetry lines recounted, battery 285/285 (279 N + 5 D + control).\\n- PROCESS: a new post-lock arm textually identical to the entry arm breaks the entry row's anchor count AND silently converts its kill into a reroute (the post-lock arm refuses the same verdict); the entry killer now asserts the admission never ran, pinning the refusal to the entry site. A shared-loop narrowing needs a killer per entry or one side is attribution-by-assertion.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev6 — attach/quiesce ordering contract; closure-authority escalation\\n\\n- P1-B FIXED: attach now revalidates the quiesce barrier under `Lifecycle.barrierMu` immediately before committing its writable client receipt, holding the lock through the receipt, the returned vector, and the advisory memory record; quiesce holds the same lock across engine closure plus report commit, boundary across its report commit only (the wait blocks on the wrapper signal). Contract: report commits and receipt commits are mutually exclusive, whichever lands first wins, no writable receipt commits after a durable closure report. Three committed tests: paused-admission late attach refuses, plus quiesce/boundary overlap tests that launch attach from inside the report write via the state crash seam and assert it blocks then refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-barrier-recheck` and `N-ordering-lock-{attach,quiesce,boundary}` (instance-scoped) all KILLED; symmetry attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1.\\n- P1-A ESCALATED (structural, not a fourth guard): a lost outcome-report write after committed engine closure still admits a fresh writable attach until retry heals the report, because admission consults the outcome proof alone and pending-vs-committed is unrepresentable there. Bound B43 names owner `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` and the scoped contract (completed-closure enumeration distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed); row 79 now claims only the lost state-record write fails closed. Same window covers receipt/report crash and double loss. B42 states the in-process bound on the ordering lock (cross-process needs a lock file) and that the covered vector handoff ends at construction.\\n- P2-A CLOSED: three read-error arms now fail closed through `Execute(attach)` with tests plus reviewer-shaped narrowings — incarnation EISDIR-as-absence (`N-incarnation-read-absent`), outcomes ENOTDIR-as-absence (`N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`), outcome-file EISDIR skip via `.json`-symlink-to-dir (`N-outcome-file-read-skip`) — and the attach entry of the unsafe-root gate carries its own valid-body test plus `N-attach-entry-root-custody` (weakened attach is served, proving admission rather than rerouting).\\n- P2-B CLOSED: importer outcome corpus now covers 36/36 packages (198 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 7 declared candidate-only; 6/6 stable runs) with `cloneproject.Normalize` no-fetcher/no-sink refusals, `sshtransport.New(zero)` invalid-snapshot refusal, and `crashgate.Lookup` known/unknown rows. Suite-verdict grid: 23,874 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 505 candidate-only additions, 0 fails.\\n- P3 CLOSED: Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates × 11 = 1540; total census 255 measured of 5248 with 186 bounds and 4807 unreachable, verified by script); row 72 lease-members prose corrected to the ownership-neutral authorization; README quiesce claim narrowed to report-committed refusal plus B43; battery counts updated (281 tmuxserver rows: 277 narrowing + 3 supplementary + control).\\n- PROCESS: an overlap test that consumes the attach result inside the hook then re-waits on the same channel hangs 10s under the lock-removal plant; putting the result back keeps the kill fast with two failure lines. Copying the outcome-grid driver into a tree breaks `go test ./...` via the specdoc no-product-command gate — run the driver, remove the directory, then run the suite.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### BUG-260917-3lddu0 — superseded leases are refused before append admission\\n\\n- FIX: `Repository.AppendEvent` now calls `checkWinningLease` after loading the durable lease winner and before `checkAppend`. Lower-epoch events refuse `ErrStaleLease`; same-epoch losing leases refuse `ErrDivergentBranch`. Refused branch bytes remain immutable and addressable, while the authoritative chain is unchanged. Historical replay intentionally does not apply this owner-side gate.\\n- REPRO: the exact trunk baseline at `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2` was driven through an adapted production `AppendEvent` probe: a successor won while the tail still named A, then A's append returned `err=<nil>` and the negative expected stale refusal. The archived review probe 15 records the old blast radius verbatim: losing-lease `profile.changed` drove `profile=yolo` with mapping `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. The candidate test `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` now refuses the append and proves `Run` cannot use that source.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 12204,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3051,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
