` (pre-commit auth failures execute the first effect; post-commit still refuse), killing through both terminate and restore entries with per-entry attribution. Census: 256 measured of 5248 (generation EXA U1→M), symmetry lines recounted, battery 285/285 (279 N + 5 D + control).\\n- PROCESS: a new post-lock arm textually identical to the entry arm breaks the entry row's anchor count AND silently converts its kill into a reroute (the post-lock arm refuses the same verdict); the entry killer now asserts the admission never ran, pinning the refusal to the entry site. A shared-loop narrowing needs a killer per entry or one side is attribution-by-assertion.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev6 — attach/quiesce ordering contract; closure-authority escalation\\n\\n- P1-B FIXED: attach now revalidates the quiesce barrier under `Lifecycle.barrierMu` immediately before committing its writable client receipt, holding the lock through the receipt, the returned vector, and the advisory memory record; quiesce holds the same lock across engine closure plus report commit, boundary across its report commit only (the wait blocks on the wrapper signal). Contract: report commits and receipt commits are mutually exclusive, whichever lands first wins, no writable receipt commits after a durable closure report. Three committed tests: paused-admission late attach refuses, plus quiesce/boundary overlap tests that launch attach from inside the report write via the state crash seam and assert it blocks then refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-barrier-recheck` and `N-ordering-lock-{attach,quiesce,boundary}` (instance-scoped) all KILLED; symmetry attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1.\\n- P1-A ESCALATED (structural, not a fourth guard): a lost outcome-report write after committed engine closure still admits a fresh writable attach until retry heals the report, because admission consults the outcome proof alone and pending-vs-committed is unrepresentable there. Bound B43 names owner `internal/terminstance ReceiptStore` and the scoped contract (completed-closure enumeration distinguishing pending-without-completion from completed); row 79 now claims only the lost state-record write fails closed. Same window covers receipt/report crash and double loss. B42 states the in-process bound on the ordering lock (cross-process needs a lock file) and that the covered vector handoff ends at construction.\\n- P2-A CLOSED: three read-error arms now fail closed through `Execute(attach)` with tests plus reviewer-shaped narrowings — incarnation EISDIR-as-absence (`N-incarnation-read-absent`), outcomes ENOTDIR-as-absence (`N-outcomes-dir-read-absent`), outcome-file EISDIR skip via `.json`-symlink-to-dir (`N-outcome-file-read-skip`) — and the attach entry of the unsafe-root gate carries its own valid-body test plus `N-attach-entry-root-custody` (weakened attach is served, proving admission rather than rerouting).\\n- P2-B CLOSED: importer outcome corpus now covers 36/36 packages (198 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 7 declared candidate-only; 6/6 stable runs) with `cloneproject.Normalize` no-fetcher/no-sink refusals, `sshtransport.New(zero)` invalid-snapshot refusal, and `crashgate.Lookup` known/unknown rows. Suite-verdict grid: 23,874 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 505 candidate-only additions, 0 fails.\\n- P3 CLOSED: Table C recounted from the Table D gate set (140 gates × 11 = 1540; total census 255 measured of 5248 with 186 bounds and 4807 unreachable, verified by script); row 72 lease-members prose corrected to the ownership-neutral authorization; README quiesce claim narrowed to report-committed refusal plus B43; battery counts updated (281 tmuxserver rows: 277 narrowing + 3 supplementary + control).\\n- PROCESS: an overlap test that consumes the attach result inside the hook then re-waits on the same channel hangs 10s under the lock-removal plant; putting the result back keeps the kill fast with two failure lines. Copying the outcome-grid driver into a tree breaks `go test ./...` via the specdoc no-product-command gate — run the driver, remove the directory, then run the suite.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### BUG-260917-3lddu0 — superseded leases are refused before append admission\\n\\n- FIX: `Repository.AppendEvent` now calls `checkWinningLease` after loading the durable lease winner and before `checkAppend`. Lower-epoch events refuse `ErrStaleLease`; same-epoch losing leases refuse `ErrDivergentBranch`. Refused branch bytes remain immutable and addressable, while the authoritative chain is unchanged. Historical replay intentionally does not apply this owner-side gate.\\n- REPRO: the exact trunk baseline at `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2` was driven through an adapted production `AppendEvent` probe: a successor won while the tail still named A, then A's append returned `err=<nil>` and the negative expected stale refusal. The archived review probe 15 records the old blast radius verbatim: losing-lease `profile.changed` drove `profile=yolo` with mapping `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. The candidate test `TestLosingLeaseProfileEventIgnored` now refuses the append and proves `Run` cannot use that source.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 12204,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3051,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
