{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d92f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":2802,"recorded_at":1780531400005599,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9c4-b5eb-70e3-89e9-4bd0e2ca31e2"},"task_id":"01a0c9c4-b5eb-70e3-89e9-4bd0e2ca31e2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9c4-b5eb-70e3-89e9-4bd0e2ca31e2","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/c28dz/conformance.md`.\n(519 line(s) above)\n520|## Bounds (mirrored B22-B44 plus carried dispositions)\n521|\n522|- B22 Singleton arms ship no narrowing mutant: admitting the\n523|  singleton refused member is deleting the gate. Covered sites, each\n524|  test-pinned in both directions where a fork exists: create relay\n525|  transport (relay), descriptor presence fork (descpresence),\n526|  attach admission nil (serveadmitnil), spawner runner nil\n527|  (spawnnil), reconcile verifier nil (reconcilenil), states root\n528|  empty (stateopen), persist/attach stores nil (storenil),\n529|  failed-kill self-confirm (selfconfirm), live-after-escalation\n530|  (stoptimeout), and post-wait boundaries without a configured\n531|  revalidation (recheckPostWait nil). The outcome-lookup empty-key\n532|  arm left this bound: it narrows now (LookupOutcomeRefusesForgedKey /\n533|  N-outcome-key-forged). Owner: this leaf; retest if any site\n534|  grows a second refused member.\n535|- B23 The landed status engine normalizes backend error details to\n536|  \"status observation unknown\" (coded or not), so the cutrow and\n537|  empty-panes narrowings measure at the helper entries while the\n538|  dispatch legs pin the code. Owner: this leaf; retest if the\n539|  engine stops normalizing.\n540|- B24 The idempotency-store Completed read-failure arm is unstaged:\n541|  no seam fails receipt reads (hooks fire on write paths only).\n542|  Owner: hardening; stage with a read-failure seam to measure.\n543|- B25 The Bind clean-miss sub-arm is unstageable: every Bind error\n544|  the hooks stage leaves the committed file, so Lookup always finds\n545|  it. The clean-found sub-arm is measured (N-bind-hook-found).\n546|  Owner: hardening.\n547|- B26 The attach effect-failure dispatch mapping is unstaged: no\n548|  committed failure reaches it (the store replays identical\n549|  receipts; conflicting receipts are untested at dispatch).\n550|  Owner: hardening.\n551|- B27 No committed test composes the Production Dependencies into\n552|  Acquire: AFG reaches the adapter and bind gates only through\n553|  caller-injected implementations (the 18 Table C U2c cells). The\n554|  injection seam is first-leaf-owned; Production wiring is\n555|  unit-pinned (TestProductionWiresDependencies). Owner: composition\n556|  test, sibling scope.\n557|- B28 The backend command-error wrap is unmeasured at PFX (no\n558|  backend test stages a refused build; the builder rows pin the\n559|  refused shapes at CMD). Owner: this leaf; retest with a\n560|  refused-build backend test.\n561|- B29 The close-confirm poll deadline is pinned for past-deadline\n562|  at PFX via direct staging; the exact-boundary member and\n563|  dispatch-level staging are unmeasured (the fake runner advances\n564|  no time). Owner: hardening.\n565|- B30 The OSRunner exit/transport/argv mappings are total functions\n566|  over uncoded inputs with no refused class to admit a member of;\n567|  tests pin them including real-exec scrub, stderr-capture, and\n568|  signal-death integrations. The signal-death arm (a killed child\n569|  errors instead of reporting -1 data) is a refused class and\n570|  carries its own narrowing row; the remaining mappings stay total.\n571|  Owner: this leaf.\n572|- B31 The custody root-ownership arm is untested and singleton: the\n573|  ownership seam stages leaf-first (the leaf refuses before the\n574|  root arm runs), and a truly foreign root needs privilege. Owner:\n575|  hardening with a privileged stage or a root-level seam.\n576|- B32 The leaf-delegation wiring is measured at CUS (wrong-leaf\n577|  mutants are observable only on compliant roots); the absence\n578|  propagation through the six dispatch paths, the prober, and the\n579|  spawner is pinned by absence tests without a row. Owner: this\n580|  leaf.\n581|- B33 The wrapper safe-boundary signal step is unimplemented in the\n582|  landed wrapper: the boundary entry waits blocking on\n583|  `ax-boundary-<generation>` for the wrapper's `wait-for -S`, and\n584|  the wrapper never signals today, so boundary waits time out with\n585|  the coded quiesce_timeout (fail closed, never a faked proof)\n586|  until the signal step lands. The wait vector, the proof-kind\n587|  binding, the provider-row context, and the timeout are this\n588|  leaf's and fully driven; the signal emission is the wrapper's.\n589|  Owner: the wrapper (`ax pane`) task; retest the full\n590|  quiesce-boundary-stop flow when the signal lands.\n591|- B34 A crash between the mutation-receipt commit and the operation\n592|  outcome record re-observes the report time on retry: the effect\n593|  never re-runs and the evidence never changes, but the reported\n594|  closure/boundary time renders from the retry clock instead of\n595|  the original one. Sequential retries without a crash replay\n596|  identical times. Before the retry heals the report, input can\n597|  reopen: attach consults the outcome proof, so the missing report\n598|  reads as no closure (bound B43 states the owner and the scoped\n599|  contract for the structural fix). Owner: this leaf for the\n600|  timestamp behavior; the receipt owner for the authority window.\n601|- B35 The absence stderr markers are verified against tmux 3.6a\n602|  (`can't find session`, `can't find window`, and the\n603|  no-such-socket connect error); any other version's\n604|  absence-shaped stderr fails closed to unknown. Owner: this leaf;\n605|  re-verify the marker set when the tmux floor version moves.\n606|- B36 The Execute dispatch and the ExecuteWrapperRestore entry pin\n607|  their dependency singletons without per-arm narrowing rows: a\n608|  nil lifecycle or a nil Runner, Receipts, Bindings, Attach,\n609|  States, CurrentLease, CurrentGeneration, or Now refuses\n610|  protocol-error before any decision or effect. Admitting one nil\n611|  arm is deleting the check. Owner: this leaf; retest if any site\n612|  grows a second refused member.\n613|- B37 No production mesh lease-refresh transport exists:\n614|  LeaseRefresh is an injected adapter (function field), and the\n615|  after-restore composition enforces the configured bound on any\n616|  adapter — cooperative or not — and rejects late answers even\n617|  with a nil error. The mesh RPC transport that would back a\n618|  production adapter is sibling scope (the mesh story); until it\n619|  lands, callers that need verified refreshes inject their own.\n620|  Owner: the mesh-refresh composition; retest the bound when a\n621|  production adapter lands.\n622|- B38 Union-rival ambiguity is unmodeled at the after-restore\n623|  composition: the entry decides over the single refreshed or\n624|  local winner, and a refresh adapter that observes rivals must\n625|  surface them as refresh failure so the entry parks unverified.\n626|  Owner: the mesh-refresh composition; retest when rivals are\n627|  modeled.\n628|- B39 Reachable-undriven: the entry reaches the gate but the\n629|  committed tests carry post-gate values only, so the refused\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
