{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d96b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":2832,"recorded_at":1780531400005659,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9c4-d401-7820-acbb-f58c1a262fe9"},"task_id":"01a0c9c4-d401-7820-acbb-f58c1a262fe9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9c4-d401-7820-acbb-f58c1a262fe9","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/c28dz/conformance.md`.\n(628 line(s) above)\n629|  committed tests carry post-gate values only, so the refused\n630|  direction is undriven at that entry; the narrowed direction is\n631|  measured at the listed entry (\"M at ...\"). Formerly claimed\n632|  unreachable as U2b; stated as a bound now. Owner: this leaf;\n633|  drive a direction to move its cell to M.\n634|- B40 Lost incarnation rotation with a prior closure stays\n635|  closed with no production-entry recovery: the failed rotation\n636|  fails the operation closed, identical retries replay success\n637|  without rotating (rotating on replay would erase a genuine\n638|  newer closure), and a fresh key is unreachable because the\n639|  landed bootstrap store binds one bootstrap per session and the\n640|  receipt store refuses a second operation under a replayed key.\n641|  The stuck closure is over-strict in the safe direction; the\n642|  committed tests pin the failure, the replay skip, and the\n643|  bootstrap-store mechanism. A lost rotation with no prior\n644|  closure is harmless (the zero incarnation stays\n645|  self-consistent). Owner: axpane receipt/bootstrap contracts\n646|  for a repair entry; operator surgery clears the superseded\n647|  reports until one lands.\n648|- B41 The restore replay rotation skip is structural: the replay\n649|  branch contains no rotation code, so no narrowing mutant can\n650|  weaken it — the supplementary additive row\n651|  D-restore-replay-rotation inserts the forbidden write to prove\n652|  the committed replay test observes it. The create-side skip\n653|  has a narrowing row (N-create-replay-skip) because its\n654|  freshness condition is explicit code. Owner: this leaf; the\n655|  asymmetry is stated, not hidden.\n656|- B42 The input-closure ordering contract is in-process: the\n657|  barrier mutex serializes quiesce/boundary report commits\n658|  against attach receipt commits within one Lifecycle, but\n659|  concurrent ax processes racing attach against quiesce observe\n660|  only the report files, so a receipt committed in another\n661|  process's report-write window is not excluded. No committed\n662|  test stages two processes. Owner: this leaf; closing the\n663|  window needs cross-process exclusion (for example a lock file\n664|  under the state root). The vector handoff the contract covers\n665|  ends at vector construction: a caller that execs a\n666|  pre-quiescence vector after quiescence commits holds a\n667|  pre-quiescence authorization, which quiesce does not revoke.\n668|  The same in-process scope covers the attach post-lock\n669|  generation and deadline rechecks: a rotation landing between\n670|  the recheck and the commit — inside one process or across\n671|  processes — is not excluded; the window holds no waits.\n672|- B43 Closure authority has no single durable source. The engine\n673|  commits input closure and its receipt before this leaf records\n674|  the outcome report, and attach admission consults the outcome\n675|  proof alone, so a lost outcome-report write after committed\n676|  closure admits a fresh writable attach until the identical\n677|  retry heals the report: the failure to create the proof reads\n678|  as permission, and pending-versus-committed closure is not\n679|  representable in the outcome store. The same window covers a\n680|  crash between the receipt commit and the report, and a\n681|  simultaneous loss of both the report and the state record.\n682|  Retrying the identical quiesce heals the report and re-closes\n683|  input; no other production entry heals it. Closing the window\n684|  structurally needs the landed receipt owner\n685|  (internal/terminstance ReceiptStore) to expose\n686|  completed-closure enumeration — the completed quiesce/boundary\n687|  receipts for one instance, distinguishing\n688|  pending-without-completion from completed — so that attach\n689|  admission can consult receipt completion as the authoritative\n690|  proof. Owner: internal/terminstance for the enumeration\n691|  contract; this leaf for the admission side once it lands.\n692|  Until then the construction (incarnation-scoped proof,\n693|  advisory-memory split, in-process ordering) stands, and row 79\n694|  claims only the lost state-record write fails closed.\n695|- B44 Attach overlap is inferred from stored receipts, not\n696|  liveness: a recorded peer reads as possibly live, so the overlap\n697|  gate requires multi_attach (and multiple_input_clients for\n698|  concurrent input) even when the peer already detached, with\n699|  same-client retries exempt and unreadable peers failing closed.\n700|  The active-client census that refines the possibility —\n701|  overlap admission over live clients, with same-client retry\n702|  distinguished from a new client — is owned by\n703|  TASK-260922-vcx6yo (active-client-census-and-overlap-admission).\n704|  Until it lands this leaf fails closed (over-strict) rather than\n705|  admitting overlap without the capabilities. Owner:\n706|  TASK-260922-vcx6yo for the census; this leaf for the fail-closed\n707|  gate.\n708|\n709|Carried bounds (first-leaf statements dispositioned by this leaf).\n710|B9 adapter split is discharged: the production exec, dial, probe,\n711|and spawn adapters ship (exec.go, probe.go, backend.go) and\n712|Production wires them into Dependencies; the residual is the\n713|uncomposed wiring (B27). B16 nested invocation is decided: lifecycle\n714|entries take no Ambient input, so nesting cannot collide through\n715|them (row 90); the Acquire-level over-strict nested refusal stands\n716|unchanged as first-leaf-owned. B18 sun_path is decided: strict-below\n717|per platform, counted in bytes (row 66). B19/B20 bind step is built:\n718|CheckSocketCustody enforces placement, leaf delegation, root,\n719|ancestors, and socket kind (rows 67-70); the bind step refuses\n720|intermediate symlinks through no-follow opens, which is stricter\n721|than the B11 Acquire rule it stands beside. The rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy\n722|foreground attach wiring is closed: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning\n723|refuses every catalog-derived decoy alone and together on the\n724|foreground running path with a spawn spy silent on every member, and\n725|the attach attestation cells carry N-attach-attestation-decoy. New\n726|bounds this revision: B33 states the unimplemented wrapper boundary\n727|signal (fail-closed timeout until it lands), B34 the receipt/outcome\n728|crash window, B35 the tmux-version marker set, B36 the dependency\n729|singletons, B38 the unmodeled union rivals, and B39 the\n730|reachable-undriven reclass. Revision 4 fills B37 (no production\n731|mesh refresh transport; the composition enforces the bound on any\n732|injected adapter), extends Table E with the binding, expiry, race,\n733|and enforcement outcomes, and moves the SPW rootwrite cell from\n734|B39 to measured. Revision 5 makes the incarnation-scoped closure\n735|proof the sole barrier verdict (new Table D rows\n736|barrierincarnation, barrierkey, attachhealth, failurerecord,\n737|createincarnation, restoreincarnation, incarnationrecord,\n738|incarnationlookup), extends Table E with the five composed-binding\n739|refusals, moves the PRB rootwrite cell from B39 to measured, and\n740|states B40 (stuck rotation) and B41 (structural replay skip).\n741|Revision 6 adds the post-admission barrier recheck with the\n742|in-process ordering lock (new Table D rows recheck and ordering;\n743|attach 1 / quiesce 1 / boundary 1), the barrier read-error arms\n744|(new Table D row barrierread; directory-read 1 / file-read 1),\n745|moves the incarnationlookup EXA cell from B39 to measured, extends\n746|the rootwrite EXA cell with the attach entry row, recounts Table C\n747|from the Table D gate set (140 gates, 1540 cells), narrows row 79\n748|to the lost state-record write with the outcome-report window\n749|stated as B43 (receipt-owner enumeration contract), and states B42\n750|(in-process ordering). Revision 7 closes the attach\n751|admission-to-effect interval for every remaining live fact (the\n752|post-lock generation and deadline rechecks with the full fact\n753|enumeration; the authorization facts revalidate inside the\n754|commit), moves the generation EXA cell from U1 to measured,\n755|extends the deadline and authkind cells with the new rows,\n756|reclassifies the two effect-loop authkind wirings as\n757|supplementary D rows beside the genuine shared loop narrowing\n758|N-lifecycle-loop-authorization, converts the entry authkind rows\n759|to genuine no-bind narrowings, and extends B42 to the new\n760|rechecks. Revision 8 closes the stop admission-to-effect interval\n761|at the escalation boundary and the quiesce interval between its\n762|commands (new Table D row effectrecheck; stop 4 / quiesce 4),\n763|bounds every barrier and admission wait by the operation deadline\n764|and cancellation (new Table D row waitbound; EXA 1 / EXE 1\n765|shared), enforces the attach overlap capabilities fail-closed\n766|over the stored peer census (new Table D rows overlapmulti and\n767|overlapinput; liveness owned by TASK-260922-vcx6yo as B44),\n768|reclassifies the entry-deadline instant row as\n769|shadowed-supplementary (the wait bound refuses the same member),\n770|extends B22 with the nil-recheck singleton, and recounts Table C\n771|from the Table D gate set (144 gates, 1584 cells).\n772|\n773|## Mutant battery\n774|\n775|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3\n776|internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`: 293/293 rows as\n777|expected (286 narrowing `N-*` KILLED plus 5 supplementary\n778|`D-*` KILLED (3 additive + 2 positive-path wiring), 1\n779|supplementary `D-*` SURVIVED-shadowed, and the shared\n780|harmless control SURVIVED), run in\n781|four chunks with one raw log per\n782|plant in the evidence tarball. The second leaf owns 213\n783|narrowing rows net (216 added, 3 reclassified). Multi-entry rows list every entry their\n784|killers cover, attribution verified per test from the raw\n785|logs (see the row notes).\n786|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3\n787|internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py`: 41/41 rows as expected\n788|(39 narrowing plus 1 supplementary plus the control),\n789|including the 4 reboot-successor rows and the peer-census row.\n790|Singleton refusal arms\n791|ship no row by bound B22 (the outcome-lookup empty-key arm\n792|left that set by narrowing); engine-normalized status details\n793|measure at the helper by bound B23; reachable-undriven cells\n794|are bound B39, not claimed unreachable.\n795|\n796|## Crash, idempotency, and determinism\n797|\n798|Every mutating operation replays the identical request without\n799|new execs (idempotency tests, one per mutating op); uncertain\n800|receipts reconcile through status before resuming (resume\n801|tests for effect failure, recheck failure, and\n802|otherwise-proven status); tampered and corrupt replays refuse\n803|(per-member tamper table, corrupt-image, hook-failure tests);\n804|reboot restore mints a deterministic successor generation and\n805|converges on retry after a crash between effects and persist.\n806|No committed test execs a real tmux or dials a real tmux\n807|server socket: the scripted runner and staged sockets are the\n808|only tmux the suite sees (one dialer test dials a synthetic\n809|local listener it creates itself, not a tmux server), and the\n810|suite passes with no tmux installed\n811|(bound B1). The three wrapper refresh tests plus the five wait\n812|tests measure wall-clock time against release-controlled\n813|instants or generous guards (enforcement is timing by\n814|definition); every other test runs on the manual clock.\n815|\n816|## Validation and evidence\n817|\n818|Configured suite green firsthand on the tree (gofmt, build,\n819|vet, full suite, race on both touched packages, cover,\n820|tracecheck, cataloggen, specdoc, linux/windows builds);\n821|334/334 mutant rows as expected across both harnesses with one\n822|raw log per plant. Raw logs:\n823|`TASK-260830-1c28dz_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.","final_result":true}}}
