{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000db87","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":3102,"recorded_at":1780531400006199,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"call_id":"call_01a0c9c6c3e170a49d647ae8d2417b5f","text":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2359 line(s) above)\n2360|mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-2056mm`. The package\n2361|adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability\n2362|claim; the clause-to-test matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n2363|[the task evidence map](internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2364|\n2365|## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\n2366|\n2367|[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\n2368|directories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or\n2369|default-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 3.2, 4.2, 4.C-4.E).\n2370|The dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC\n2371|root (per-user temporary directory on macOS, `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax` on\n2372|Linux/WSL2), resolved by the landed `localstore` layout and supplied by\n2373|the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity.\n2374|`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root\n2375|handle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three\n2376|independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\n2377|ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\n2378|verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\n2379|server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\n2380|override on all five ambient members (`TMUX` and `TMUX_TMPDIR`\n2381|environment values, inherited socket, default path, conventional\n2382|`default` name). `Acquire` reaches the server through the\n2383|caller-appropriate path: foreground ensures the directory, then attaches\n2384|to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S` server whose\n2385|stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while background\n2386|verifies the existing directory without creating it, contacts only the\n2387|already-running authenticated same-user broker and its attested server,\n2388|and a miss — including an absent runtime directory, the ordinary\n2389|post-reboot cold state — returns the typed `capability_unavailable`\n2390|refusal with realm/readiness details, while an existing-but-unsafe\n2391|directory keeps its custody refusal — there is no fallback to direct\n2392|creation, and every background-path `Acquire` test (24/24 by\n2393|mechanical census) arms both a spy spawner and a spy server probe\n2394|that fail the run if either is ever invoked. Attestation is the landed `terminalbackend`\n2395|Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission consumed as an `Admitted` set\n2396|composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\n2397|stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\n2398|live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\n2399|runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\n2400|process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request. Lifecycle\n2401|operations — create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop,\n2402|stale termination, restore — run through structured argv builders over\n2403|the dedicated socket: `Execute` admits exactly the eight operations\n2404|and refuses unknown ones, the exec adapter reconstructs the exact\n2405|`tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation and refuses\n2406|forged binaries, flag injection, and ambient socket discovery, and\n2407|the probed socket generation is bound (B18-B20) before any execution.\n2408|Bodies are pure argv builders whose stable pane entrypoint stays\n2409|`ax pane SESSION_ID`; effects run through the landed terminstance\n2410|engine with strict per-operation deadlines, per-effect generation\n2411|and authorization rechecks, and AX-side state memory for\n2412|reconciliation, while attach, terminate, and restore mirror the\n2413|landed backend, fencing, and axpane gates. Destructive commands\n2414|that follow a wait revalidate first: the stop escalation\n2415|re-proves deadline, authorization, and generation after its poll\n2416|before the kill issues (a graceful timeout escalates; any other\n2417|stale fact refuses), and the quiesce detach revalidates between\n2418|the commands; every barrier and admission wait honors the\n2419|operation deadline and cancellation with no late commit. Attach\n2420|additionally fails closed on overlap: a second client that may\n2421|overlap a recorded peer needs multi_attach, and new input over a\n2422|recorded input peer needs multiple_input_clients, with\n2423|same-client retries exempt; client liveness is bound B44 in the\n2424|traceability map (owned by TASK-260922-vcx6yo). Quiesce\n2425|cuts operator input by locking then detaching every attached client\n2426|and refusing new input-authorized attaches at the entry once its\n2427|closure report commits (read-only observation stays); a lost report\n2428|after committed closure is bound B43 in the traceability map. The\n2429|boundary waits blocking for the wrapper\n2430|signal with the proof kind bound into its evidence; probes prove\n2431|absence only from marked tmux stderr and read every other failure as\n2432|unknown. Every mutating operation replays the identical request\n2433|idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before\n2434|resuming.\n2435|\n2436|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n2437|\n2438|```bash\n2439|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\n2440|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\n2441|```\n2442|\n2443|Run the narrowing battery (286 narrowing mutants, six supplementary\n2444|rows — three additive, two positive-path wiring, and one shadowed\n2445|entry-deadline narrowing that survives by reroute to the wait\n2446|bound — plus one harmless control) with:\n2447|\n2448|```bash\n2449|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\n2450|```\n2451|\n2452|The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n2453|through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n2454|reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n2455|additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\n2456|raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n2457|attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`, with the lifecycle battery and its\n2458|raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. The package adds\n2459|no `ax` command, no\n2460|`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\n2461|matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n2462|[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2463|\n2464|## Ownership reducer properties\n2465|\n2466|The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\n2467|and 13.6-13.10) hold as executable property tests over the landed production\n2468|reducers — `sessstate.Reduce` with `Compare` and the union projection,\n2469|`sessrepo.WinningLease` with `ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`:\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
