{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dc4b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":3200,"recorded_at":1780531400006395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9c7-32a6-7c30-9929-12d03bb669f7"},"task_id":"01a0c9c7-32a6-7c30-9929-12d03bb669f7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9c7-32a6-7c30-9929-12d03bb669f7","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-61-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 12 LOGBOOK.md; echo ...; grep -n \\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -n 5\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed\\n\\n- P1-A FIXED (stop escalation + quiesce mid-sequence): the stop escalation revalidates the operation deadline, AX authorization over the live lease, and server generation after its poll before `kill-session` issues — a graceful timeout escalates, any other stale fact refuses without the kill — and the quiesce detach revalidates between the lock and detach commands. The two post-wait boundaries share one closure over the landed gates (same `CheckAuthorization` call, same generation read, row's own timeout code) with per-site skip narrowings; sibling paths probed with fact-mutation during their waits: create/restore single-command (rotation changes nothing), terminate tail (kill count stays one, refusal stands), boundary tail (post-signal command is the read-only rows probe). Graceful wait and operation deadline are distinct bounds. Narrowings: 3 shared arms + 2 per-site skips, all KILLED with per-test attribution; census effectrecheck stop 4 / quiesce 4.\\n- P2 FIXED (bounded waits, uniform barrier contract): the attach admission and barrier acquisition run under one wait context combining the operation deadline with caller cancellation — the entry bounds the wait itself (goroutine + select, late answers discarded), so even a non-cooperative adapter cannot hold the request past its deadline or commit late. Quiesce span and boundary report commit acquire through the same contract (row's own timeout code; boundary reports against its committed proof). Release-controlled tests prove refusal-before-release plus no-late-receipt; cancellation returns promptly. Narrowing `N-attach-wait-deadline` KILLED through all four deadline tests while the cancellation companion stays green.\\n- P1-B NARROWED (overlap fail-closed): this leaf has no liveness census, so a stored peer receipt reads as possibly live — a second client needs `multi_attach`, new input over an input peer needs `multiple_input_clients`, same-client retries exempt, unreadable peers fail closed. Over-strict by design (detached clients' receipts still trigger) until the liveness census lands; owner TASK-260922-vcx6yo, stated as B44. Narrowings `N-attach-overlap-multi` / `-input` KILLED with two-peer precision legs. The §4.C attach row claims only the fail-closed gate, never liveness.\\n...\\n8:### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed\\n17:### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev7 — attach effect-boundary enumeration; authkind evidence repair\\n26:### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev6 — attach/quiesce ordering contract; closure-authority escalation\\n57:### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\\n61:- Full 30-command suite green firsthand on the frozen tree (gofmt, build, vet, full suite, race gate, cover, all fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/windows builds, JSON check, board validate, diff check, windows vet); OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate importer comparison clean (base 82 PASS retained, zero regressions). Evidence tarball with raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3356,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 839,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
