{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dc7f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c9a4-cdaf-7691-9123-20534004d71c"},"sequence":3226,"recorded_at":1780531400006447,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7d4d0da9-54d0-407b-9491-ce60f372e27f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c9c7-626c-7c43-9dde-f5f42f7b66fe"},"task_id":"01a0c9c7-626c-7c43-9dde-f5f42f7b66fe","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c9c7-626c-7c43-9dde-f5f42f7b66fe","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-22\n-\n-### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed\n+## 2026-09-22\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev9 — census integrity, in-flight probe bounds, validated replay, attribution repair\n+\n+- P1 FIXED (receipt-namespace directory fails closed): the peer census skipped every directory before reading, so a directory at the exact `<client-UUID>.json` receipt path read as no peers and admitted a second client without `multi_attach`. The census now skips only staging (`attach-*`) and non-receipt names; any other entry — including a directory — must read as a valid receipt file or the attach refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-peers-dir` (termbind) and `N-attach-peers-dir-skip` (tmuxserver, cross-package plant) KILLED through the census test and the entry test; new census row peershape.\n+- P2-A FIXED (read-only probes honor the deadline in-flight): the stop poll, the terminate-stale self-confirm, and the status live probes ran under the caller's context while the deadline lived only in a field/clock checks, so a blocked probe waited past the bound. One shared `probeContext` (duration-derived, fake-clock-safe: answered probes follow the clock exactly, only never-answered probes conclude by the context) now bounds all three; expiry concludes unknown, never a verdict. Release-controlled entry tests pin refusal-before-release with no kill/closure/termination/report. Shared narrowing `N-probe-deadline` KILLED through all three entries with isolated single-test attribution. Runner audit: every other wait/probe is deadline-bounded (barrier/admission/boundary/dial); single-shot commits stay caller-cancellation-bounded as stated bound B45 (engine-mirrored; a hung commit hangs, never mis-verdicts).\n+- P2-B NARROWED (receipt-validated replay with a peer present): the overlap gate demanded overlap capabilities before consulting the durable store, so an identical same-client retry with another peer present refused `capability_unproven`. A Lookup-proven recorded receipt now exempts the retry (replay, or `idempotency_mismatch` when transport/input changed, after the live authorization recheck); a client with no recorded receipt still gates however it names itself. Pin: input + read-only replay shapes with an input peer, plus the conflicting-retry mismatch leg. Narrowing `N-attach-overlap-replay-unproven` KILLED; census row overlapreplay; B44 clarified (validated replay here, liveness with TASK-260922-vcx6yo).\n+- P2-D REPAIRED (isolated kill attribution): the three shared escalation/wait plants claimed per-entry kills the fixtures could not deliver (quiesce auth subtest at exact expiry under the -1h plant; strictly-past deadline case vs the equal-instant narrowing; boundary-commit 7h advance vs the +1h widening). Fixtures now drive the admitted class (30-min-past expiry, on-deadline instant leg, 6.5h advance with release-controlled barrier) and every shared plant kills through every claimed killer ALONE, twice, with the companion/precision legs green — stop 4 / quiesce 4 and 4 wait killers measured, not claimed. Census: 148 gates, 266 measured of 5504 (pollbound measured; terminate tail corrected U1→B39); battery 296/296 + 42/42.\n+- P2-C REPAIRED (evidence freshness): the rev9 evidence archive is built from the frozen rev9 tree and attached with its absolute path, then read back and digest-verified from the board — the stale-archive failure is closed by construction, not by prose.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed\n","final_result":true}}}
